[2026-07-20T17:13:35.642Z] [INFO]           "prompt": "Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843 (repo link-assistant/formal-ai, branch issue-812-7f9674a82402). Do NOT commit or push anything. Read-only investigation plus writing ONE markdown report.\n\nContext: The \"Desktop Release\" workflow (.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml) fails on `Build macos-x64` and `Build macos-arm64` with:\n\n```\n⨯ Command failed: codesign --sign - --force --timestamp=none --options runtime --entitlements build/entitlements.mac.plist \\\n  .../formal-ai Desktop.app/Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/Frameworks/Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework\n.../Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework: replacing existing signature\n.../Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework: unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\n```\n\nFull logs are at dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/ci-logs/run-29752745259.log (3.6MB; grep it, read in chunks). Prior analysis of the same defect (labelled \"Defect B\") is in dev/log/issues/810/pulls/811/analysis.md — READ IT FIRST, sections 3 and 8. Prior instrumentation lives in desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.cjs and its test desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.test.cjs.\n\nEstablished by prior iteration: the custom sign hook IS invoked, the `ignore` predicate IS consulted, and @electron/osx-sign DOES skip paths under Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/... So the failing codesign invocation is NOT coming from the walked-children path that our ignore predicate governs.\n\nYour job: find WHO issues that codesign command if osx-sign skips it. Concretely:\n1. Read desktop/package.json (electron-builder config), desktop/scripts/*.cjs, any afterPack/afterSign hooks, and how browser-runtime gets into Contents/Resources (extraResources? a download step?).\n2. Inspect the installed electron-builder / app-builder-lib / @electron/osx-sign sources under desktop/node_modules (if present) to determine the code path that signs `Contents/Resources/**/Frameworks/*.framework` — look for `opts.binaries`, `signAsync`, the `--deep`/framework enumeration, and electron-builder's own `MacPackager` re-sign of the outer bundle after the hook returns. Note exact file:line references.\n3. In run-29752745259.log, find the ordering: which sign phase emits the failing line, whether `[adhoc-sign-mac]` banner/counter lines appear at all in THIS run (grep \"adhoc-sign-mac\"), and what `considered=`/`skipped=` report.\n4. Explain \"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\" precisely: what layout rule codesign enforces for embedded .framework bundles, and why the Chrome for Testing framework as shipped violates it once it is nested inside another app bundle. Search online (WebSearch/WebFetch) for electron-builder / puppeteer / playwright issues about bundling Chrome for Testing inside a .app and codesign sealing — cite URLs.\n5. Check whether existing libraries/components solve this (e.g. @electron/osx-sign ignore semantics, electron-builder `asarUnpack`, `extraResources` with archives, puppeteer browser download at runtime, `@puppeteer/browsers`). Cite URLs.\n6. Propose ranked, concrete fixes with the actual code/config diff sketch for each, and say which is structural rather than a workaround.\n\nWrite your report to dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis/macos-codesign.md. Be rigorous: every claim either cites a log line number, a file:line, or a URL. Say plainly what remains unproven. Final message: a 20-line summary of root cause + recommended fix."
