[2026-07-20T17:13:38.041Z] [INFO]         "type": "tool_result",
[2026-07-20T17:13:38.041Z] [INFO]         "content": "1\t# Issue #810 — CI/CD false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors\n2\t\n3\tSession: `issue-810-claude-20260720`\n4\tPull request: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/811\n5\t\n6\t## 1. Evidence collected\n7\t\n8\t| Artifact | Path |\n9\t| --- | --- |\n10\t| Desktop Release run 29738571290 (full log) | `ci-logs/run-29738571290.log` |\n11\t| Desktop Release run 29738571290 (job metadata) | `ci-logs/run-29738571290.json` |\n12\t| CI/CD Pipeline run 29737218421 (full log) | `ci-logs/run-29737218421.log` |\n13\t| CI/CD Pipeline run 29737218421 (job metadata) | `ci-logs/run-29737218421.json` |\n14\t\n15\tBoth runs are on the default branch at `bd0bac88` (the merge of #809), the exact\n16\tcommit named in the issue body.\n17\t\n18\tFailing jobs:\n19\t\n20\t| Run | Job | Conclusion |\n21\t| --- | --- | --- |\n22\t| 29737218421 (CI/CD Pipeline) | Auto Release | failure |\n23\t| 29738571290 (Desktop Release) | Build macos-arm64 | failure |\n24\t| 29738571290 (Desktop Release) | Build macos-x64 | failure |\n25\t| 29738571290 (Desktop Release) | Publish SHA256SUMS.txt + provenance | failure (cascade) |\n26\t\n27\tEvery other job in both runs passed. There are exactly **two** independent\n28\tdefects; the third failure is a downstream consequence of the second.\n29\t\n30\t## 2. Defect A — the self-hosting evidence gate deadlocked every release\n31\t\n32\t### Symptom\n33\t\n34\t`ci-logs/run-29737218421.log:27173`:\n35\t\n36\t```\n37\tAuto Release  Collect changelog and bump version\n38\t  Error recording self-hosting release metric: no committed Formal-AI-Evidence\n39\t  in 10e65ae2a22f206589ecba9974c95151e0124bc3 records session issue-804-claude-20260720\n40\t  ##[error]Process completed with exit code 1.\n41\t```\n42\t\n43\t### Root cause\n44\t\n45\t`scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs` attributes a commit to Formal AI only when the\n46\tdocument named by its `Formal-AI-Evidence` trailer contains the literal session\n47\tid from its `Formal-AI-Session` trailer (`commit_has_formal_ai_evidence`, around\n48\tline 142). Commit `10e65ae2` records:\n49\t\n50\t```\n51\tFormal-AI-Session: issue-804-claude-20260720\n52\tFormal-AI-Evidence: dev/log/issues/804/pulls/805/analysis.md\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\tbut that document never spells its own session id out. Verified locally:\n56\t\n57\t```\n58\t$ git show 10e65ae2:dev/log/issues/804/pulls/805/analysis.md | grep -c issue-804-claude-20260720\n59\t0\n60\t```\n61\t\n62\tThe check therefore returns `Err`, and `measure()` propagates it, aborting the\n63\twhole `Auto Release` job.\n64\t\n65\t### Why it was not caught before merge — the timeline\n66\t\n67\t1. `10e65ae2` is authored and merged as part of PR #805. The pull-request run\n68\t   for that branch (`29722531797`, head `8f5edf3a`) shows **no**\n69\t   `Self-Hosting Evidence Check` job in its job list — the gate did not exist\n70\t   yet.\n71\t2. `39fdef91` (\"gate evidence trailers in PRs\") adds the `evidence-check` job to\n72\t   `.github/workflows/release.yml`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor` confirms\n73\t   `39fdef91` lands **after** `10e65ae2`.\n74\t3. `10e65ae2` is now immutable history on `main`.\n75\t4. `record_release` measures `<last tag>..HEAD`. `10e65ae2` sits inside that\n76\t   range and will keep sitting there **until a new tag is cut**.\n77\t5. Cutting a new tag requires `Auto Release` to succeed. `Auto Release` aborts on\n78\t   `10e65ae2`.\n79\t\n80\tThat is a closed loop: the release cannot run because of a commit, and the only\n81\tthing that would move the range past that commit is a successful release. Every\n82\t`Auto Release` on `main` fails forever, with no possible fix in new commits.\n83\t\n84\tThis is a **false negative turned permanent outage**: a policy gate applied\n85\tretroactively to history that predates it.\n86\t\n87\t### Fix applied\n88\t\n89\t`scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs` grows an explicit `EvidencePolicy`:\n90\t\n91\t- `Strict` — used by `measure()`, i.e. the pull-request `evidence-check` gate. A\n92\t  malformed evidence record is a hard error, rejected *before* it can reach the\n93\t  default branch. Enforcement is unchanged where enforcement is actionable.\n94\t- `Lenient` — used by `record_release()`. A malformed record is reported on\n95\t  stderr as `warning: not attributing <sha>: <reason>` and the commit simply is\n96\t  not counted as self-authored. Its lines still count toward `changed_lines`.\n97\t\n98\tThe metric can therefore only ever *under*-report self-hosting, never\n99\tover-report it, so the ratchet stays honest while a release can no longer be\n100\theld hostage by history.\n101\t\n102\t### Regression test\n103\t\n104\t`tests/unit/specification/self_hosting_metric.rs::a_malformed_historical_evidence_record_cannot_deadlock_a_release`\n105\tbuilds a fixture repo containing exactly the shape of `10e65ae2` (evidence that\n106\tmentions `formal-ai` but never names its session), then asserts both halves:\n107\t`measure()` still returns `Err`, and `record_release()` succeeds with\n108\t`self_authored_commits == 0` and `commits == 1`.\n109\t\n110\t```\n111\ttest specification::self_hosting_metric::a_malformed_historical_evidence_record_cannot_deadlock_a_release ... ok\n112\ttest result: ok. 5 passed; 0 failed\n113\t```\n114\t\n115\t### Follow-up worth considering\n116\t\n117\tThe gate would be more useful if it *generated* rather than *checked*: have the\n118\tsolver template write `Formal-AI-Session: <id>` into the evidence document\n119\titself, so the trailer and the document cannot drift apart. Requiring a human or\n120\tan agent to duplicate an identifier in two places is the actual defect generator\n121\there.\n122\t\n123\t## 3. Defect B — macOS ad-hoc signing breaks the bundled Chrome framework seal\n124\t\n125\t### Symptom\n126\t\n127\t`ci-logs/run-29738571290.log:6976` (identically at `:14883` for `macos-x64`):\n128\t\n129\t```\n130\telectron-osx-sign Executing... codesign --sign - --force --timestamp=none\n131\t  --options runtime --entitlements build/entitlements.mac.plist\n132\t  .../formal-ai Desktop.app/Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/Frameworks/Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework\n133\t> Stderr: ...: replacing existing signature\n134\t         ...: unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\n135\t  ⨯ Command failed: codesign ...   failedTask=build\n136\t```\n137\t\n138\t`Publish SHA256SUMS.txt + provenance` then fails as designed\n139\t(`log:16680`: \"No artifacts from: macos-x64 macos-arm64\") — that job is behaving\n140\tcorrectly and needs no change.\n141\t\n142\t### What the evidence does and does not establish\n143\t\n144\tEstablished:\n145\t\n146\t- The custom sign hook **was** resolved and invoked. `log:4028` carries\n147\t  electron-builder's own marker, emitted only on the `customSign` branch of\n148\t  `MacPackager.doSign` (`app-builder-lib@26.15.3/out/macPackager.js:334`):\n149\t  `• executing custom sign  file=release/mac-arm64/formal-ai Desktop.app`.\n150\t- `--timestamp=none` on every `codesign` line confirms our `optionsForFile`\n151\t  override was in effect, so `signAsync` was called from our module.\n152\t- The signing path that failed is the one the hook is specifically written to\n153\t  skip.\n154\t\n155\tNot established, and this is the blocker:\n156\t\n157\t- **Not a single `[adhoc-sign-mac]` line appears anywhere in the 3.9 MB log**\n158\t  (`grep -ac \"hook entered\" → 0`), even though the workflow sets\n159\t  `FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG=1` and the hook's very first statement is an\n160\t  unconditional banner. So we cannot tell whether `signingIgnoreRules()`\n161\t  returned a predicate that was consulted and answered \"sign it\", or was never\n162\t  consulted at all.\n163\t\n164\tThe two candidate root causes are therefore still open:\n165\t\n166\t1. **Output loss.** `process.stderr.write()` on a pipe — which is what GitHub\n167\t   Actions hands a child process — is asynchronous and buffered. When\n168\t   electron-builder aborts the process on the signing error, anything still\n169\t   queued is discarded. `debug`-based output from `electron-osx-sign` survived,\n170\t   which is consistent but not conclusive.\n171\t2. **The predicate genuinely did not match.** Ruled unlikely: the exported\n172\t   `signingIgnoreRules` is unit-tested against the exact failing path, and\n173\t   `@electron/osx-sign@1.3.3`'s `validateOptsIgnore` (`dist/cjs/sign.js:52`)\n174\t   wraps a bare function into `[fn]` correctly — it is only the *array* form\n175\t   that it silently drops, which is the bug #808 already worked around.\n176\t\n177\t### Instrumentation added (default state unchanged)\n178\t\n179\tPer the \"add debug output so the next iteration can find it\" instruction:\n180\t\n181\t- `log()` now writes through `fs.writeSync(2, ...)` instead of\n182\t  `process.stderr.write()`. A synchronous write to fd 2 cannot be lost to an\n183\t  aborting process. This eliminates candidate 1 outright: if the banner is still\n184\t  missing next run, the module is not the one executing.\n185\t- `signingIgnoreRules()` attaches a `stats` counter to the predicate, and the\n186\t  hook reports `ignore predicate: considered=N skipped=M` in a `finally` block —\n187\t  so it is emitted on failure as well as success. `considered=0` and\n188\t  `skipped=0` mean very different things and one line now distinguishes them.\n189\t- The per-file `ignore SKIP/sign ...` trace stays behind\n190\t  `FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG`, **off by default**, exactly as before. Only the\n191\t  two summary lines are unconditional.\n192\t- Regression test:\n193\t  `desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.test.cjs::the ignore predicate counts what it\n194\t  considered and what it skipped`. Full desktop sign suite: 4 passed, 0 failed.\n195\t\n196\t### Candidate fixes for the next iteration, in order of preference\n197\t\n198\t1. **Confirm and fix the ignore path** once the counters land. If\n199\t   `skipped == 0`, the predicate never ran and the fix is in how the hook passes\n200\t   `ignore`; if `skipped > 0` but the runtime was still signed, `signAsync` is\n201\t   signing it from `opts.binaries` rather than the walked children.\n202\t2. **Do not hand codesign the framework at all.** Ship the browser runtime as an\n203\t   archive under `Contents/Resources` and expand it on first launch. `codesign`\n204\t   never walks into it, the upstream Chrome signature is preserved byte for\n205\t   byte, and the failure mode disappears structurally rather than by\n206\t   configuration. Cost: a first-run extraction step and its error handling.\n207\t3. **Move the runtime out of the app bundle** into `Application Support`,\n208\t   downloaded or expanded on demand. Smallest bundle, largest behavioural\n209\t   change.\n210\t\n211\tOption 2 is the one that removes the class of bug rather than the instance —\n212\t\"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\" is\n213\t`codesign` correctly refusing to co-sign a bundle it did not lay out, and no\n214\tamount of ignore-rule tuning changes that. Worth doing regardless of what the\n215\tcounters show.\n216\t\n217\t### Upstream reporting\n218\t\n219\tNo upstream issue is warranted yet. The `@electron/osx-sign` array-vs-function\n220\t`ignore` bug is real and already documented in-repo at\n221\t`desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.cjs`, but it is a known upstream behaviour that\n222\t#808 worked around; a report should wait until the counters tell us whether the\n223\tremaining failure is upstream's or ours. Filing now would be filing a guess.\n224\t\n225\t## 4. Requirement checklist from the issue\n226\t\n227\t| # | Requirement | Status |\n228\t| --- | --- | --- |\n229\t| 1 | Collect all logs/data into `dev/log/issues/810/pulls/811` | Done — 10 MB of run logs plus job metadata |\n230\t| 2 | Deep analysis, timeline, root cause per problem | Done — §2 and §3 |\n231\t| 3 | Fix false positives / false negatives / warnings / errors | Defect A fixed and tested; Defect B instrumented, not yet fixed |\n232\t| 4 | Add debug output + verbose mode, default off, when data is short | Done — §3, per-file trace remains behind `FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG` |\n233\t| 5 | Report upstream issues where applicable | Assessed, deliberately deferred — §3 |\n234\t| 6 | Apply each fix everywhere it occurs | Defect A: single call site (`record_release`), verified by grep across `scripts/*.rs`. Defect B: single hook, shared by both mac jobs |\n235\t| 7 | Compare against the three CI/CD pipeline templates | **Not done** — see §5 |\n236\t\n237\t## 5. Known gap\n238\t\n239\tRequirement 7 (a file-by-file comparison against\n240\t`link-foundation/{rust,js,python}-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`, and\n241\treporting anything found back to those templates) has not been carried out in\n242\tthis pass. Neither of the two observed failures originates in template-derived\n243\tworkflow structure — Defect A is repo-specific policy tooling and Defect B is\n244\trepo-specific desktop packaging — so the template sweep is genuinely separate\n245\twork rather than a prerequisite for the fixes above. It should not be marked\n246\tcomplete until someone diffs the workflows.\n247\t\n248\t---\n249\t\n250\t## 6. Second iteration — two nondeterministic failures on the PR branch\n251\t\n252\tRun [29742025207](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/actions/runs/29742025207)\n253\t(head `70a09859`) failed two jobs that pass on `main`. Neither is caused by the\n254\tbranch's diff (which touches only `scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs` and its test):\n255\tboth are **flakes**, i.e. false negatives, which requirement 3 of the issue\n256\tcovers explicitly. Evidence: `ci-logs/coverage.log`, `ci-logs/e2e.log`,\n257\t`ci-logs/formal-ai-serve-8776.log`, `ci-logs/agent-out-8776.log`. The six most\n258\trecent `main` runs fail only in `Auto Release` (Defect A), never in these jobs.\n259\t\n260\t### Defect C — `desktop_release_resolve` unit test, ETXTBSY on the mock `gh`\n261\t\n262\t```\n263\tci_cd::desktop_release_resolve::workflow_run_skips_when_release_has_all_required_assets\n264\t  left: \"true\"   right: \"false\"\n265\t```\n266\t\n267\t`1937 passed; 1 failed`, and the same test passes locally and in every earlier\n268\trun. The test writes a mock `gh` into a scratch `PATH` directory and immediately\n269\texecutes it. The unit suite is multi-threaded: any `Command` spawn in another\n270\ttest thread forks this process, and a fork landing between the mock's `write`\n271\tand its `close` inherits the still-open write descriptor. `execve` on an inode\n272\tthat any process holds open for writing fails with `ETXTBSY`. The resolve script\n273\tswallows a failed `gh` (`|| true`), so the asset query degrades silently to \"no\n274\tassets exist\" and `should_build` flips to `true` — exactly the observed values.\n275\t\n276\tFixes:\n277\t\n278\t* The mock is written to `gh.staging` and `rename`d into place, so the name that\n279\t  gets executed is never the file being written (`tests/unit/ci-cd/desktop_release_resolve.rs`).\n280\t* `scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh` no longer conflates \"`gh` failed\" with\n281\t  \"the release has no assets\": it keeps the query's exit status and logs a\n282\t  warning. The decision is unchanged (both still build — the fail-safe\n283\t  direction); only the diagnosis improves.\n284\t* The assertion now prints the script's stdout, which carries the\n285\t  `existing desktop assets: N` / `missing required desktop assets` lines.\n286\t\n287\t### Defect D — agent CLI E2E, auto-compaction swallowed the report prompt\n288\t\n289\t```\n290\t!! report request did not execute gh\n291\t```\n292\t\n293\t`formal-ai-serve-8776.log` shows the whole sequence. The research turn fetched\n294\tthree live pages (fec.gov, usatoday, wikipedia) and grew the transcript to a\n295\t246 KB request. opencode then issued a *summarisation* request (\"You are a\n296\thelpful AI assistant tasked with summarizing conversations\"), and the next turn\n297\tarrived at the server with last user message `\"Continue if you have next steps\"`\n298\t— not `\"Report this problem\"`. The server logged\n299\t`agentic_outcome: fallthrough (task unrecognised)`, no `gh` ran, and the\n300\tassertion failed for a reason unrelated to the behaviour under test.\n301\t\n302\tRoot cause: the harness advertised a 200000-token context limit, and transcript\n303\tsize depends on whatever the live pages happen to serve that day — so whether\n304\tcompaction triggers is a property of the public web, not of this repository.\n305\t\n306\tFix (`experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_687.sh`): raise the advertised limit to\n307\t4000000. It is a harness knob only — the server never enforces it — so this\n308\tremoves the live-content dependency rather than masking a product defect. A\n309\tdiagnostic branch now also names compaction explicitly when the `gh` log is\n310\tmissing and the server log contains a summarisation request, so the two failure\n311\tmodes are never again confused.\n312\t\n313\t## 7. Template sweep (requirement 7)\n314\t\n315\tCloned `link-foundation/{rust,js,python}-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`\n316\tand diffed their workflows against `.github/workflows/{release,desktop-release}.yml`,\n317\tthen re-checked both against\n318\t`link-assistant/hive-mind/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`.\n319\t\n320\tAlready matching the templates, verified line by line: concurrency groups with\n321\t`cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}`, `GIT_CONFIG_*`\n322\tdefault-branch hint suppression, least-privilege `permissions: contents: read`\n323\twith per-job escalation, `timeout-minutes` on every job, `detect-changes`\n324\tfast-fail ordering, secrets scan, version-check, and attest-before-upload.\n325\t\n326\tActed on:\n327\t\n328\t* **False negative — desktop dry run missed Rust changes.** `desktop-release.yml`'s\n329\t  pull-request `paths` filter listed only `desktop/**`, `vscode/**` and two\n330\t  scripts, yet the build job runs `cargo build --release --bin formal-ai` and\n331\t  bundles that binary. A Rust-only change could break desktop packaging with a\n332\t  green PR. `src/**`, `Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock` are now in the filter.\n333\t\n334\tChecked and rejected:\n335\t\n336\t* The `for f in release/latest*.yml; do [ -f \"$f\" ] && files+=(\"$f\"); done` loops\n337\t  (`desktop-release.yml` collect/upload steps) were flagged as a `set -e` abort\n338\t  when the last file is absent. They are not: bash exempts a failing command\n339\t  that is part of an `&&` list. Verified directly —\n340\t  `bash -c 'set -euo pipefail; for f in a b; do [ -f \"$f\" ] && echo yes; done; echo ALIVE'`\n341\t  prints `ALIVE`.\n342\t* `finalize`'s `if: always() && … should_build == 'true'` was flagged as letting\n343\t  a failed `resolve` pass silently. It does not: a failed job fails the run\n344\t  regardless of what the downstream job does.\n345\t\n346\tStill open (recorded, not done — each is a refactor rather than a fix):\n347\t\n348\t* The js template's `check-file-line-limits` job covers `.md` and `release.yml`;\n349\t  our `scripts/check-file-size.rs` covers only `.rs`, `.lino` and worker `.js`.\n350\t  `release.yml` is 1791 lines, over the documented 1500-line ceiling, with\n351\t  nothing failing.\n352\t* `simulate-fresh-merge.sh` runs in `lint` and `test` but not in\n353\t  `desktop-release.yml`, so the packaging dry run builds the PR head rather than\n354\t  the merge result.\n355\t\n356\t## 8. Defect B: the `ignore` predicate is confirmed to be consulted\n357\t\n358\tThe PR description recorded this as unknown: \"it is still unknown whether the\n359\t`ignore` predicate was consulted and said 'sign it' or was never called -- the\n360\ttwo need different fixes.\" The instrumentation added in this PR answers it.\n361\t\n362\tEvidence: `ci-logs/desktop-29746221627.log` (Desktop Release run 29746221627,\n363\tjob \"Build macos-x64\", step \"Package desktop app (macOS ad-hoc)\").\n364\t\n365\t* The hook banner now emits, so the hook itself runs:\n366\t  `[adhoc-sign-mac] hook entered (debug=on)` followed by\n367\t  `[adhoc-sign-mac] signOptions keys: app, binaries, identity, identityValidation, ignore, keychain, optionsForFile, platform, preAutoEntitlements, provisioningProfile, strictVerify, type, version`.\n368\t* The predicate is called, once per candidate path, e.g.\n369\t  `[adhoc-sign-mac] ignore sign root=.../Contents/Resources/browser-runtime relative=../../Frameworks/Electron Framework.framework/... path=...`.\n370\t* `@electron/osx-sign` acts on the answer: every path inside\n371\t  `Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/Frameworks/Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework/...`\n372\t  is logged by osx-sign as `Skipped...`, including the Helper `.app` bundles,\n373\t  `libwidevinecdm.dylib`, `Assets.car` and the `Versions/Current` aliases.\n374\t\n375\tSo the remaining macOS seal failure is not \"the predicate was never called\" and\n376\tnot \"the predicate said sign it\" for the browser runtime -- that path is\n377\tcorrectly excluded. `candidate appPath: null` / `candidate path: null` in the\n378\tsame log show electron-builder passes the bundle only as `signOptions.app`,\n379\twhich is why the earlier root-derivation attempts read as undefined.\n380\t\n381\tCaveat on scope: pull request desktop builds are ad-hoc/unsigned dry runs, so\n382\tthe \"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\"\n383\tcodesign error is not reproduced here. This evidence narrows the cause; it does\n384\tnot close Defect B, which stays instrumented and open by design.\n385\t"
