reported upstream. For (d) draft a ready-to-file issue body with a reproducible example, workaround and code-level fix suggestion — put those drafts in the report, do not file them.\n6. Pay particular attention to: shell safety (`set -euo pipefail`, unquoted vars, `|| true` swallowing failures), steps that can pass while doing nothing (false positives), `continue-on-error`, `if: always()` misuse, missing `timeout-minutes`, missing concurrency groups, permissions scope, action version pinning (SHA vs tag), cache keys, matrix fail-fast, artifact retention, and any grep/test that silently succeeds on empty input.\n7. Also save copies of the three templates' workflow files into dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/templates/<template-name>/ for the record.\n\nWrite your report to dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis/template-sweep.md with a findings table (ID, file:line, class, severity, evidence, proposed fix). Every finding must cite file:line. Final message: a prioritized list of the top findings."
