[2026-07-20T17:14:50.977Z] [INFO]         "content": "1398\t          EXPECT_FILE: google-trends-learning.lino\n1399\t          EXPECT_TEXT: human_gated\n1400\t          MIN_POSTS: 3\n1401\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n1402\t\n1403\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — general unpinned change plan (issue #654)\"\n1404\t        # No `*_TASK` constant names this request. The fallback planner derives the\n1405\t        # target, literal payload, evidence, and verification command from the\n1406\t        # formalized requirement, writes its plan event first, then executes it.\n1407\t        env:\n1408\t          PORT: 8773\n1409\t          TASK: \"Create file artifacts/general-agent-plan.txt containing general planner e2e passed\"\n1410\t          EXPECT_FILE: artifacts/general-agent-plan.txt\n1411\t          EXPECT_TEXT: general planner e2e passed\n1412\t          MIN_POSTS: 4\n1413\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n1414\t\n1415\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — file-creation routes to write not read (issue #681)\"\n1416\t        # The exact reproduction from issue #681: a \"create a file … with the\n1417\t        # content …\" request used to emit a `read` on the not-yet-existing target\n1418\t        # and finish with \"File not found\", writing nothing. Driven live through\n1419\t        # the real CLI, the request must now walk the write/create plan (write plan\n1420\t        # → write target → verify → final = 4 posts) and leave hello.txt on disk\n1421\t        # carrying its content — never a read of the file it was asked to create.\n1422\t        env:\n1423\t          PORT: 8775\n1424\t          TASK: \"Create a file named hello.txt with the content hello world\"\n1425\t          EXPECT_FILE: hello.txt\n1426\t          EXPECT_TEXT: hello world\n1427\t          MIN_POSTS: 4\n1428\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n1429\t\n1430\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — existing issue reference does not file a duplicate (issue #730)\"\n1431\t        # Use wording different from the captured case-study run. Mentioning an\n1432\t        # existing issue beside a file request must drive the complete write plan,\n1433\t        # never the report router's real `gh issue create` side effect.\n1434\t        env:\n1435\t          PORT: 8781\n1436\t          TASK: \"For existing issue-730, create file issue-730-finding.md containing provenance paths are portable\"\n1437\t          EXPECT_FILE: issue-730-finding.md\n1438\t          EXPECT_TEXT: provenance paths are portable\n1439\t          MIN_POSTS: 4\n1440\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n1441\t\n1442\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — capability-first local code search (issue #758)\"\n1443\t        env:\n1444\t          PORT: 8782\n1445\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_758.sh\n1446\t\n1447\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — generated programs use harness commands (issue #716)\"\n1448\t        # The exact screenshot reproduction must create the source in the real\n1449\t        # Agent CLI workspace, then ask that harness to compile and run it. The\n1450\t        # request trace preserves both shell calls so a prose-only response or\n1451\t        # server-private execution cannot satisfy this check.\n1452\t        env:\n1453\t          PORT: 8776\n1454\t          TASK: \"Give me hello world program in Rust\"\n1455\t          EXPECT_FILE: main.rs\n1456\t          EXPECT_TEXT: \"Hello, world!\"\n1457\t          MIN_POSTS: 4\n1458\t          EXPECT_SERVER_TEXTS: |-\n1459\t            rustc main.rs -o main\n1460\t            ./main\n1461\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n1462\t\n1463\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — auto-learn client execution architecture (issue #716)\"\n1464\t        # Replay the same investigation through Formal AI's associative-memory\n1465\t        # adapter and real Agent CLI tools. The report remains review-gated; its\n1466\t        # evidence links make the architectural promotion auditable.\n1467\t        env:\n1468\t          PORT: 8777\n1469\t          TASK: \"Use Formal AI auto-learning to inspect the persisted issue 716 client-execution failures as an associative links network, rank the observations and architectural amendments, keep promotion human-review gated, and write client-execution-learning-report.lino.\"\n1470\t          EXPECT_FILE: client-execution-learning-report.lino\n1471\t          EXPECT_TEXT: \"lesson:typed-execution-artifact\"\n1472\t          MIN_POSTS: 3\n1473\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n1474\t\n1475\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — declarative new-file phrasing (issue #712)\"\n1476\t        # The exact declarative shape from issue #712 previously fell through to\n1477\t        # the read router. The live CLI must execute the complete write plan and\n1478\t        # leave the requested file behind, proving this is more than a response-\n1479\t        # serialization fix.\n1480\t        env:\n1481\t          PORT: 8776\n1482\t          TASK: \"new file: notes.txt, contents: hello\"\n1483\t          EXPECT_FILE: notes.txt\n1484\t          EXPECT_TEXT: hello\n1485\t          MIN_POSTS: 4\n1486\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n1487\t\n1488\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — report action executes gh (issue #714)\"\n1489\t        timeout-minutes: 3\n1490\t        env:\n1491\t          PORT: 8780\n1492\t        run: experiments/issue_714_agentic_mode/run_report_e2e.sh\n1493\t\n1494\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — research, report, recall, and learn (issue #687)\"\n1495\t        # Continue four natural-language turns in one real Agent CLI session.\n1496\t        # A PATH-local fake gh proves shell execution without mutating GitHub.\n1497\t        env:\n1498\t          PORT: 8776\n1499\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_687.sh\n1500\t\n1501\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — filed report stays readable and bounded (issue #771)\"\n1502\t        # The reported session answered a question from a whole scraped page and\n1503\t        # then filed it, producing a 51KB issue whose transcript escaped its own\n1504\t        # markdown. Asserts over the real transport that every turn stays inside\n1505\t        # an attributed block and the body fits GitHub's issue size limit.\n1506\t        env:\n1507\t          PORT: 8781\n1508\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_771.sh\n1509\t\n1510\t      - name: \"Run four-client E2E — narrated compatibility research (issue #781)\"\n1511\t        # The exact reported marketplace question drives Agent, OpenCode,\n1512\t        # Claude Code, and Codex through their native transports. Each trace\n1513\t        # must show a narrated search, three separately narrated fetch turns,\n1514\t        # and a cited synthesis. Per-dialog JSONL preserves every exchange.\n1515\t        env:\n1516\t          PORT: 8783\n1517\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_781.sh\n1518\t\n1519\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — auto-learning across two harnesses (issue #715)\"\n1520\t        # The derived report names its own promotion gate\n1521\t        # `..._and_agent_cli_e2e_pass`, so the gate is only honest if a real\n1522\t        # external Agent CLI runs the task — until this step it had only ever run\n1523\t        # in formal-ai's own in-process harness. Driving both CLIs and diffing the\n1524\t        # two reports byte for byte is what makes \"all harnesses supported in the\n1525\t        # similar way\" an assertion instead of a claim.\n1526\t        timeout-minutes: 5\n1527\t        env:\n1528\t          PORT: 8879\n1529\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_715_learning.sh\n1530\t\n1531\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — self-hosting auto-learning (issue #657)\"\n1532\t        # The self-hosting metric measures the share of a release Formal AI\n1533\t        # authored, so deriving its own learning report only inside formal-ai's\n1534\t        # in-process harness would test the claim with the one harness that\n1535\t        # cannot show it. Here formal-ai serves as the model provider for both\n1536\t        # external CLIs — Formal AI executing issue #657's task using Formal AI,\n1537\t        # with no external model and no API key — and the two reports must match\n1538\t        # byte for byte.\n1539\t        timeout-minutes: 5\n1540\t        env:\n1541\t          PORT: 8881\n1542\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_657_metric.sh\n1543\t\n1544\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — hardcoded-language auto-learning (issue #659)\"\n1545\t        # Formal AI is the model provider while two external Agent CLIs execute\n1546\t        # a differently worded version of issue #659's learning task. Both must\n1547\t        # derive the same review-gated artifact from persisted evidence.\n1548\t        timeout-minutes: 5\n1549\t        env:\n1550\t          PORT: 8882\n1551\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_659_learning.sh\n1552\t\n1553\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — bulk-lexeme auto-learning (issue #660)\"\n1554\t        # Formal AI is the model provider while two external Agent CLIs derive\n1555\t        # the same review-gated lessons from issue #660's persisted evidence.\n1556\t        timeout-minutes: 5\n1557\t        env:\n1558\t          PORT: 8883\n1559\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_660_learning.sh\n1560\t\n1561\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — handler-precedence auto-learning (issue #663)\"\n1562\t        # Formal AI serves as the model provider while the real Agent CLI\n1563\t        # executes a differently-worded version of issue #663's learning task and\n1564\t        # re-derives the specialized-handler precedence itself. The authored\n1565\t        # report must match the byte-for-byte committed evidence.\n1566\t        timeout-minutes: 5\n1567\t        env:\n1568\t          PORT: 8885\n1569\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_663_learning.sh\n1570\t\n1571\t      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — repository statement audit (issue #661)\"\n1572\t        # The real Agent CLI delegates the repository scan to the public release\n1573\t        # binary in its own workspace, then consumes the command result before\n1574\t        # finishing. The artifact must expose weights, provenance-backed\n1575\t        # findings, requirement conflicts, and learned associations.\n1576\t        timeout-minutes: 5\n1577\t        env:\n1578\t          PORT: 8884\n1579\t        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_661_statement_audit.sh\n1580\t\n1581\t      - name: \"Replay Hive Mind self-coding inner loop (issue #655)\"\n1582\t        env:\n1583\t          PORT: 8774\n1584\t        run: |\n1585\t          examples/self-coding/run.sh\n1586\t          cargo test self_coding_session_replays\n1587\t\n1588\t      - name: Upload E2E logs on failure\n1589\t        if: failure()\n1590\t        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7\n1591\t        with:\n1592\t          name: agent-cli-e2e-logs\n1593\t          path: |\n1594\t            /tmp/formal-ai-serve-*.log\n1595\t            /tmp/agent-out-*.log\n1596\t          retention-days: 7\n1597\t\n1598\t  # === DEPLOY WEB APP ===\n1599\t  # Deploy the production web app from src/web/ to GitHub Pages after a successful build.\n1600\t  deploy-pages:\n1601\t    name: Deploy Web App to GitHub Pages\n1602\t    needs: [build, auto-release, manual-release]\n1603\t    outputs:\n1604\t      page_url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}\n1605\t      pages_sha: ${{ steps.pages_ref.outputs.sha }}\n1606\t    if: |\n1607\t      !cancelled() &&\n1608\t      needs.build.result == 'success' && (\n1609\t        (github.event_name == 'push' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && needs.auto-release.result == 'success') ||\n1610\t        (github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' && github.event.inputs.release_mode == 'instant' && needs.manual-release.result == 'success')\n1611\t      )\n1612\t    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n1613\t    # 20 min (was 15): this job now also runs `cargo doc` for the /docs/api\n1614\t    # reference, which compiles the dependency tree on a cold cargo cache.\n1615\t    timeout-minutes: 20\n1616\t    permissions:\n1617\t      contents: read\n1618\t      pages: write\n1619\t      id-token: write\n1620\t    environment:\n1621\t      name: github-pages\n1622\t      url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}\n1623\t    steps:\n1624\t      - name: Select Pages deployment ref\n1625\t        id: pages_ref\n1626\t        env:\n1627\t          PAGES_DEPLOY_SHA: ${{ needs.auto-release.outputs.pages_sha || needs.manual-release.outputs.pages_sha || github.sha }}\n1628\t        run: |\n1629\t          if [ -z \"$PAGES_DEPLOY_SHA\" ]; then\n1630\t            echo \"::error::Could not resolve Pages deployment SHA\"\n1631\t            exit 1\n1632\t          fi\n1633\t          echo \"sha=${PAGES_DEPLOY_SHA}\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n1634\t          echo \"Pages deployment SHA: ${PAGES_DEPLOY_SHA}\"\n1635\t\n1636\t      - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n1637\t        with:\n1638\t          ref: ${{ steps.pages_ref.outputs.sha }}\n1639\t\n1640\t      - name: Configure GitHub Pages\n1641\t        uses: actions/configure-pages@v6\n1642\t\n1643\t      - name: Setup Bun\n1644\t        uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@v2\n1645\t        with:\n1646\t          bun-version-file: .bun-version\n1647\t\n1648\t      - name: Install web bundle dependencies\n1649\t        run: bun install --frozen-lockfile\n1650\t\n1651\t      - name: Build web vendor bundle\n1652\t        run: bun run build:web\n1653\t\n1654\t      # === API DOCS (/docs/api) ===\n1655\t      # The documentation hub (/docs/) links to a Rust API reference at\n1656\t      # /docs/api/. Generate it with `cargo doc` here and copy it into the Pages\n1657\t      # artifact below so it deploys alongside the rest of the site (issue #479).\n1658\t      - name: Setup Rust\n1659\t        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\n1660\t\n1661\t      # Reclaim runner disk before the heavy doc build: `cargo doc` plus the web\n1662\t      # bundle, the docs copy and the Pages artifact tar need headroom, and\n1663\t      # without this the runner crashed with \"No space left on device\" (#523).\n1664\t      - name: Free up runner disk space\n1665\t        run: bash scripts/free-runner-disk.sh\n1666\t\n1667\t      # IMPORTANT (issue #523): cache only the downloaded crate sources, NOT the\n1668\t      # `target/` directory. The other Rust jobs (notably `lint`, which runs\n1669\t      # `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features`) share the same cache key and\n1670\t      # populate `target/` with a multi-gigabyte debug tree. Restoring that here\n1671\t      # on top of the web bundle and then running `cargo doc` exhausted the\n1672\t      # runner disk. `cargo doc --no-deps --lib` rebuilds its own (much smaller)\n1673\t      # `target/` from the cached registry, so we keep the registry/git cache for\n1674\t      # download speed but never restore the bloated build artifacts.\n1675\t      - name: Cache cargo registry\n1676\t        uses: actions/cache@v5\n1677\t        with:\n1678\t          path: |\n1679\t            ~/.cargo/registry\n1680\t            ~/.cargo/git\n1681\t          key: ${{ runner.os }}-cargo-docs-${{ hashFiles('**/Cargo.lock') }}\n1682\t          restore-keys: |\n1683\t            ${{ runner.os }}-cargo-docs-\n1684\t\n1685\t      - name: Generate Rust API docs (cargo doc)\n1686\t        env:\n1687\t          RUSTDOCFLAGS: -D warnings\n1688\t        run: |\n1689\t          # Document just the library (lib name: formal_ai). --no-deps keeps the\n1690\t          # output small and fast. Keep rustdoc fail-closed just like rustc so a\n1691\t          # green Pages deployment cannot conceal broken API links or markup.\n1692\t          cargo doc --no-deps --lib\n1693\t          # rustdoc emits the crate docs under target/doc/formal_ai/; add a root\n1694\t          # redirect so /docs/api/ lands on the crate root instead of 404ing.\n1695\t          cat > target/doc/index.html <<'HTML'\n1696\t          <!doctype html>\n1697\t          <html lang=\"en\">\n1698\t            <head>\n1699\t              <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n1700\t              <meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0; url=formal_ai/index.html\" />\n1701\t              <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"formal_ai/index.html\" />\n1702\t              <title>formal-ai API reference</title>\n1703\t            </head>\n1704\t            <body>\n1705\t              <p>Redirecting to the <a href=\"formal_ai/index.html\">formal-ai API reference</a>&hellip;</p>\n1706\t            </body>\n1707\t          </html>\n1708\t          HTML\n1709\t\n1710\t      - name: Sync data/seed into src/web/seed (deployment mirror)\n1711\t        run: scripts/sync-seed.sh\n1712\t\n1713\t      - name: Read formal-ai version from Cargo.toml\n1714\t        id: formal_ai_version\n1715\t        run: |\n1716\t          version=\"$(sed -n 's/^version[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' Cargo.toml | head -n 1)\"\n1717\t          if [ -z \"$version\" ]; then\n1718\t            echo \"::error file=Cargo.toml::Could not read formal-ai version from Cargo.toml\"\n1719\t            exit 1\n1720\t          fi\n1721\t          echo \"version=${version}\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n1722\t          echo \"Detected formal-ai version: ${version}\"\n1723\t\n1724\t      - name: Stamp GitHub Pages artifact\n1725\t        run: scripts/stamp-pages-artifact.sh src/web \"${{ steps.pages_ref.outputs.sha }}\" \"${{ steps.pages_ref.outputs.sha }}\" \"${{ steps.formal_ai_version.outputs.version }}\"\n1726\t\n1727\t      - name: Copy Rust API docs into the Pages artifact (/docs/api)\n1728\t        run: |\n1729\t          # Copy after stamping: rustdoc's HTML carries no version placeholders,\n1730\t          # and copying post-stamp keeps stamp-pages-artifact.sh from scanning\n1731\t          # the (large) generated tree.\n1732\t          mkdir -p src/web/docs/api\n1733\t          cp -R target/doc/. src/web/docs/api/\n1734\t\n1735\t      - name: Upload GitHub Pages artifact\n1736\t        uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v5\n1737\t        with:\n1738\t          path: src/web\n1739\t\n1740\t      - name: Deploy Pages artifact\n1741\t        id: deployment\n1742\t        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v5\n1743\t        env:\n1744\t          # deploy-pages v5 still imports core punycode. Keep every other Node\n1745\t          # warning visible while upstream issue #434 removes this dependency.\n1746\t          NODE_OPTIONS: --disable-warning=DEP0040\n1747\t\n1748\t  # === E2E TESTS (GITHUB PAGES) ===\n1749\t  # Run Playwright tests against the live GitHub Pages URL after deployment.\n1750\t  test-e2e-pages:\n1751\t    name: E2E Tests (GitHub Pages)\n1752\t    needs: [deploy-pages]\n1753\t    if: |\n1754\t      !cancelled() &&\n1755\t      needs.deploy-pages.result == 'success'\n1756\t    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n1757\t    timeout-minutes: 15\n1758\t    steps:\n1759\t      - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n1760\t\n1761\t      - name: Setup Node.js\n1762\t        uses: actions/setup-node@v6\n1763\t        with:\n1764\t          node-version: '24.x'\n1765\t          cache: npm\n1766\t          cache-dependency-path: tests/e2e/package-lock.json\n1767\t\n1768\t      - name: Install Playwright and dependencies\n1769\t        run: |\n1770\t          cd tests/e2e\n1771\t          npm ci\n1772\t\n1773\t      - name: Install Playwright browsers\n1774\t        run: |\n1775\t          cd tests/e2e\n1776\t          npx playwright install --with-deps chromium\n1777\t\n1778\t      - name: Wait for GitHub Pages deployment\n1779\t        env:\n1780\t          PAGES_DEPLOY_SHA: ${{ needs.deploy-pages.outputs.pages_sha || github.sha }}\n1781\t        run: scripts/wait-for-pages-deployment.sh \"${{ needs.deploy-pages.outputs.page_url }}\" \"$PAGES_DEPLOY_SHA\"\n1782\t\n1783\t      - name: Run GitHub Pages e2e tests\n1784\t        run: |\n1785\t          cd tests/e2e\n1786\t          PAGES_URL=\"${{ needs.deploy-pages.outputs.page_url }}\" npx playwright test --config=playwright.pages.config.js\n1787\t\n1788\t      - name: Upload Playwright report on failure\n1789\t        if: failure()\n1790\t        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7\n1791\t        with:\n1792\t          name: playwright-report-pages\n1793\t          path: tests/e2e/playwright-report/\n1794\t          retention-days: 7\n1795\t"
