[2026-07-20T17:19:17.116Z] [INFO]         "type": "tool_result",
[2026-07-20T17:19:17.116Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"electron-builder bundle puppeteer chromium inside app codesign signIgnore browser\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Codesigning fails when adding Puppeteer as a dependency · Issue #2010 · electron-userland/electron-builder\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder/issues/2010\"},{\"title\":\"Using Node.js, Puppeteer and ElectronJS to Create a Web Scraping App with a Desktop Interface | by Alex Ruma | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@alexanderruma/using-node-js-puppeteer-and-electronjs-to-create-a-web-scraping-app-with-a-desktop-interface-668493ced47d\"},{\"title\":\"Is it possible to run puppeteer on electron window? · Issue #4655 · puppeteer/puppeteer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/puppeteer/puppeteer/issues/4655\"}]\n\nThe search results provide relevant information about issues with bundling Puppeteer and Chromium in Electron apps with code signing. Here's what was found:\n\n## Key Issues and Solutions\n\nWhen adding Puppeteer as a dependency, codesigning fails since the module contains a local version of Chromium.\n\n### Codesigning Problem\nThe codesign command fails on nested Chromium Framework files within Puppeteer's local Chromium installation, with errors indicating that code objects are not signed.\n\n### Potential Fixes\nThis can be fixed by adding the --deep flag to the codesigning arguments or by preventing electron-builder from signing automatically using the CSC_IDENTITY_AUTO_DISCOVERY=false environment variable.\n\n### Alternative Approaches\nInstead of bundling Puppeteer's Chromium, you can solve this by pointing the 'executablePath' option in puppeteer.launch() directly to the location of Chromium or Chrome on the end user's machine. Chromium is already bundled into Electron itself, which could also be leveraged for your use case.\n\nThe core challenge is that Electron's code signing process has difficulty with Puppeteer's nested Chromium bundles, but there are multiple workaround strategies available depending on your specific needs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
