[2026-07-20T17:19:17.158Z] [INFO]       {
[2026-07-20T17:19:17.158Z] [INFO]         "tool_use_id": "toolu_017JnycpeBawR9NtGNSrjXnB",
[2026-07-20T17:19:17.158Z] [INFO]         "type": "tool_result",
[2026-07-20T17:19:17.158Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"\"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\" codesign\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Codesigning fails: unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework · Issue #1471 · sparkle-project/Sparkle\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sparkle-project/Sparkle/issues/1471\"},{\"title\":\"codesign: \\\"unsealed contents prese… | Apple Developer Forums\",\"url\":\"https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/93914\"},{\"title\":\"Qt Frameworks issues with MacOS notarization | Qt Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.qt.io/topic/111154/qt-frameworks-issues-with-macos-notarization\"},{\"title\":\"CodeSign fails in Xcode for embedded framework - MacOSX and iOS - JUCE\",\"url\":\"https://forum.juce.com/t/codesign-fails-in-xcode-for-embedded-framework/59372\"},{\"title\":\"FBSDKCoreKit.framework: Unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework · Issue #2130 · facebook/facebook-ios-sdk\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/facebook/facebook-ios-sdk/issues/2130\"},{\"title\":\"x/mobile/cmd/gomobile: unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework · Issue #66406 · golang/go\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/golang/go/issues/66406\"},{\"title\":\"Codesign: The Saga Continues • furbo.org - Craig Hockenberry\",\"url\":\"https://furbo.org/2020/12/01/codesign-the-saga-continues/\"},{\"title\":\"Code Signing Failure due to Symlink Folders – Indie Spark\",\"url\":\"https://indiespark.top/programming/code-signing-failure-due-to-symlink-folders/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the \"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\" codesign error:\n\n## What This Error Means\n\nThis error occurs when you try to codesign an embedded framework and Apple's codesign tool detects files or content at the root level of the framework that shouldn't be there.\n\n## Common Causes\n\nThe error typically stems from improperly structured framework bundles:\n\n1. **Files in the root directory**: There should be no regular files in the top level directory of the framework bundle. For example, Qt frameworks may have .prl files in the root directory that should be moved into the Resources subdirectory.\n\n2. **Symlink issues**: Symlinks with extended attributes (like macOS Finder information) in the framework can cause this error.\n\n3. **Incorrect bundle placement**: Bundles placed in the wrong location within a framework structure will prevent code signing from succeeding.\n\n## Solutions\n\nThe common fixes include:\n\n- Move resources from the framework root directory to the proper location (e.g., Versions/A/Resources/)\n- Ensure the framework isn't being re-signed by Xcode when embedded into your app bundle by unchecking the \"Sign\" checkbox for individual frameworks in Xcode target settings\n- Remove symlink creation scripts from your build phases\n\nThis is a common issue when embedding third-party frameworks like Qt, Sparkle, Facebook SDK, and others that don't follow Apple's strict framework structure requirements.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
