[2026-07-20T17:19:20.327Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   The single user (launching-agent) message set the whole task. Verbatim-critical constraints and instructions:\n\n   - Working directory `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843` (repo `link-assistant/formal-ai`, branch `issue-812-7f9674a82402`). \"Do NOT commit or push. Read-only investigation plus writing ONE markdown report and cloning templates to a scratch dir OUTSIDE the repo (use /tmp/templates).\"\n   - Task = requirement 7 of issue https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/812 — \"a file-by-file comparison of this repo's CI/CD against three upstream templates, to adopt best practices and to find latent false positives/false negatives.\"\n   1. Clone into /tmp/templates: `link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`, `js-...`, `python-...`.\n   2. Fetch `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` → save to `dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/templates/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`.\n   3. Compare the FULL file tree of each template's CI/CD surface (.github/workflows/**, .github/actions/**, scripts/**, composite actions, dependabot config, CI-relevant issue templates) against this repo's `.github/workflows/release.yml`, `.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml` and `scripts/**`.\n   4. \"IMPORTANT: a previous iteration already did a partial sweep. READ dev/log/issues/810/pulls/811/analysis.md section 7 first and do NOT re-report what it already covered as done; instead verify its two 'still open' items and go deeper on everything it did not cover.\"\n   5. Classify every divergence as (a) real defect in THIS repo (false positive / false negative / warning / error waiting to happen), (b) best practice worth adopting, (c) intentional difference, or (d)