 -0` exit-code propagation.\n   - secretlint (diff-scoped vs full-tree), lychee link checking, changeset/changelog.d fragments, fresh-merge simulation (stale merge preview), electron-builder macOS ad-hoc signing.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/.github/workflows/release.yml` (1794 lines) — read in full. Structure: jobs `detect-changes`(62), `changelog`(93), `evidence-check`(124), `docker-build`(159), `secrets-scan`(213), `version-check`(246), `lint`(272), `test`(487), `coverage`(563), `build`(637), `auto-release`(675), `manual-release`(929), `changelog-pr`(1148), `test-e2e-local`(1199), `test-agent-cli-e2e`(1279), `deploy-pages`(1600), `test-e2e-pages`(1750). Notable lines for findings:\n     - L35–42 concurrency `cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}` (documented, intentional; best-practices doc says `==`).\n     - L241 `BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref || github.event.before || 'HEAD~1' }}` feeding check-secrets.sh.\n     - L365 `FILE_SIZE_WARNING_BASE: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha || github.event.before }}` (empty on workflow_dispatch; rust template instead has a `Collect changed files` step with a `git ls-files` fallback).\n     - L506–510 `fail-fast: false`, `os: [ubuntu-latest]` only (template uses ubuntu/macos/windows) — documented as a speed trade-off but a false-negative source given desktop builds on macOS/Windows.\n     - L603–608 LCOV artifact with `if-no-files-found: error` (good).\n     - L610–633 Codecov detection via `CODECOV_TOKEN` secret → step output; skips upload with a `::notice::` when unset.\n     - L641/L677 `build` needs `[lint, test]`; `auto-release` needs `[lint, test, build]` — **E2E jobs (`test-e2e-local`, `test-agent-cli-e2e`) and `secrets-scan`/`docker-build` are NOT in the release gate**, so a release can publish on main while E2E fails.\n     - L913–925 and L1133–1145 `Resolve Pages deploy ref` with `if: always()` (best practice: `!cancelled()`).\n     - L1263–1271 `Upload generated /download screenshots` with `if: always()`, no `if-no-files-found` (defaults to `warn` → can pass doing nothing).\n     - L1602–1611 `deploy-pages` requires `auto-release`/`manual-release` success (rust template deliberately keeps docs deploy independent of the release path).\n     - L1735–1738 `actions/upload-pages-artifact@v5` with `path: src/web` and **no `include-hidden-files: true`** (rust template sets it at its L947).\n     - All actions pinned by tag (`@v6`, `@v7`, `@stable`), not SHA — same as templates.\n   - `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml` (704 lines) — read in full. Jobs `resolve`(91), `build`(143, 6-way matrix, `fail-fast: false`), `vscode`(499), `finalize`(585). Notable:\n     - L50–65 PR `paths` filter now includes `src/**`, `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock` (prior iteration's fix).\n     - L70–80 concurrency keyed on PR number/tag/head_sha; `cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}`.\n     - L161–164 `build` job grants `contents: write`, `id-token: write`, `attestations: write` **even for pull_request dry runs** (over-scoped).\n     - L421–451 `Collect artifacts and checksums` (has `set -euo pipefail`, empty-array guard, no `shopt -s nullglob`); L479–490 `Upload assets to release` repeats the glob loop without an emptiness guard.\n     - L591 `finalize` `if: ${{ always() && github.event_name != 'pull_request' && needs.resolve.outputs.should_build == 'true' }}` — `always()` means a **cancelled** run still publishes a partial `SHA256SUMS.txt`; best practice `!cancelled()`.\n     - L599–608 `actions/download-artifact@v8` with `pattern: checksums-*`.\n     - L629 `commit=\"$(gh release view ... --jq .targetCommitish || echo unknown)\"` — swallows failure into \"unknown\".\n     - L700–704 `Fail if any target produced no artifacts` (good pattern).\n     - **No `simulate-fresh-merge.sh` anywhere** → confirms prior analysis's still-open item (ii): the packaging dry run builds the PR head, not the merge result.\n   - `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/scripts/check-file-size.rs` — limits `.rs` 1000/900, `.lino` 1500/1400, worker `.js` 1500/1400; excludes `target`, `.git`, `node_modules`, `data/cache/wikidata/`, `dev/log/`. **No `.md` and no `.yml` coverage** → confirms still-open item (i): `release.yml` is 1794 lines vs the js template's 1500 ceiling and nothing fails.\n   - `/tmp/templates/js/scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh` — LIMIT=1500, WARN_THRESHOLD=1350, walks tracked `.js/.mjs/.cjs/.md` plus `.github/workflows/release.yml` with the hint \"Move inline scripts to the ./scripts/ folder to reduce file size.\"\n   - `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/scripts/check-secrets.sh` (86 lines) — `set -euo pipefail` at L27; `exclude()` at L39–41 uses `grep -zv ... || true`; L44–68 selects `--all` / explicit args / `BASE_REF` diff / working-tree; L55–58 falls back to `HEAD~1` when the base ref doesn't resolve (handles the all-zeroes push SHA); L70–73 exits 0 on empty file list (\"No files to scan.\" — a legitimate but explicit no-op); L80–84 `printf '%s\\0' | xargs -0 npx --yes -p secretlint -p @secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend secretlint` (unpinned npx download).\n   - `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/scripts/install-rust-script.sh` — superset of the template's: `set -euo pipefail`, short-circuit on PATH, `cargo install rust-script --locked`, configurable `RUST_SCRIPT_INSTALL_ATTEMPTS`/`..._RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS`.\n   - `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` — adopted verbatim from the **js** template. Uses `set -euo pipefail` (L21) but unquoted `origin/$BASE_REF` in `git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/$BASE_REF` and `git merge origin/$BASE_REF --no-edit`. The **rust** template's variant is materially different: quotes everything, uses `git merge-base --is-ancestor` short-circuit, merges into a *detached* checkout of the base tip, and then runs `cargo fmt/clippy/test` itself (`FRESH_MERGE_CHECKS` ove