[2026-07-20T17:19:27.971Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"\"@puppeteer/browsers\" download chromium at runtime electron app userData instead of bundling\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"puppeteer - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/puppeteer\"},{\"title\":\"@puppeteer/browsers | Puppeteer\",\"url\":\"https://pptr.dev/browsers-api\"},{\"title\":\"download-chromium - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/download-chromium\"},{\"title\":\"Is it possible to run puppeteer on electron window? · Issue #4655 · puppeteer/puppeteer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/puppeteer/puppeteer/issues/4655\"},{\"title\":\"Installation | Puppeteer\",\"url\":\"https://pptr.dev/guides/installation\"},{\"title\":\"Download Chromium\",\"url\":\"https://www.chromium.org/getting-involved/download-chromium/\"},{\"title\":\"Puppeteer | Chrome for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/puppeteer\"},{\"title\":\"@puppeteer/browsers - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@puppeteer/browsers\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding using `@puppeteer/browsers` to download Chromium at runtime in Electron apps:\n\n## Runtime Download with @puppeteer/browsers\n\nThe easiest way to download Chrome for Testing binaries for your platform is by using the @puppeteer/browsers command-line utility, available via npm.\n\n## Electron userData Path Configuration\n\nFor Electron applications specifically, you can set the install path if you can't write to your node_modules, for example from within an electron packaged app using `require('electron').app.getPath('userData')`. This allows you to avoid bundling Chromium with your app and instead download it to the user's data directory at runtime.\n\n## Custom Browser Providers\n\nYou can implement custom browser providers to download from alternative sources like corporate mirrors, private repositories, or specialized browser builds. This gives you flexibility in how and where to download the browser binaries.\n\nThe key advantage of this approach for Electron apps is that it reduces your bundle size by not including Chromium at build time, and instead allows users to download it on first run to their local userData directory.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
