[2026-07-20T17:19:48.323Z] [INFO]       {
[2026-07-20T17:19:48.323Z] [INFO]         "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Tu96Bn7dgrAHv7ggJ6W6Ry",
[2026-07-20T17:19:48.323Z] [INFO]         "type": "tool_result",
[2026-07-20T17:19:48.323Z] [INFO]         "content": "# Understanding \"unsealed contents present in root directory\"\n\nBased on the forum thread, this error message means that **codesign detected regular files (not just symlinks) in the root directory of a framework bundle**, which violates macOS framework structure requirements.\n\n## The Problem\n\nThe error occurs when a framework bundle has files in its top-level directory that should be located elsewhere. In the Qt 5.9.3 case, `.prl` files were present in the root directory:\n\n```\nQtCore.framework/\n├── Headers -> Versions/Current/Headers\n├── QtCore -> Versions/Current/QtCore\n├── QtCore_debug -> Versions/Current/QtCore_debug\n├── Resources -> Versions/Current/Resources\n├── QtCore.framework.prl  ← PROBLEM: Regular files in root\n└── Versions/\n```\n\n## What codesign Requires\n\nAccording to the solution provided, a valid embedded framework structure must have:\n\n1. **Only symlinks in the root directory** (not regular files)\n2. **An \"A\" version symlink** in the Versions directory:\n   ```\n   QtCore.framework/Versions/\n   ├── 5/\n   ├── A -> 5  ← Required by codesign\n   └── Current -> 5\n   ```\n3. **All actual files** located in the versioned subdirectory (`Versions/Current/` or similar)\n\n## The Solution\n\nThe user fixed it by:\n- Moving `.prl` files from the root into `Resources/`\n- Creating the required `A -> 5` symlink in the Versions directory\n\nThe user notes: *\"codesign is currently spitting out error messages which are simply not true, misleading and not helpful to resolve the code signing issues.\"*"
[2026-07-20T17:19:48.323Z] [INFO]       }
[2026-07-20T17:19:48.323Z] [INFO]     ]
[2026-07-20T17:19:48.323Z] [INFO]   },
