[2026-07-20T17:23:22.357Z] [INFO]         "text": "Report written. No commits or pushes made; only the report plus the previously staged template copies exist as new untracked files.\n\n**Deliverables**\n- `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis/template-sweep.md` — 23 findings (F1–F23) with file:line, class (a/b/c/d), severity, evidence, proposed fix; plus two ready-to-file upstream issue drafts.\n- `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/templates/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` and `.../templates/{rust,js,python}-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/` (all 8 template workflow + composite-action files).\n- Templates cloned to `/tmp/templates/{rust,js,python}` (outside the repo).\n\n**Prioritized top findings**\n\n1. **F3 — E2E and secret-scan jobs are outside the release gate** (`.github/workflows/release.yml:641,677-681`). `auto-release` needs only `[lint, test, build]`; `test-e2e-local` (:1199), `test-agent-cli-e2e` (:1279), `secrets-scan` (:213) and `docker-build` (:159) can be red while a crate + GitHub release publishes from main. Highest-impact false negative found.\n2. **F1 — file-size gate has no workflow-YAML or `.md` coverage** (`scripts/check-file-size.rs`). `release.yml` is 1794 lines vs the js template's 1500 ceiling and CI is green. Prior sweep item (i), confirmed still open.\n3. **F2 — desktop packaging never simulates the fresh merge** (`.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml:143-497`). `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` exists but is invoked nowhere in that workflow, so the dry run builds the PR head, not the merge result. Prior sweep item (ii), confirmed still open.\n4. **F4 — `finalize` uses `always()`** (`desktop-release.yml:588-591`): a *cancelled* desktop release still `--clobber`s `SHA256SUMS.txt`/`BUILD-PROVENANCE.txt` with a partial manifest. js template explicitly warns against this (hive-mind #1278).\n5. **F13/F5 — silently-empty inputs**: `FILE_SIZE_WARNING_BASE` is empty on `workflow_dispatch`/first push (`release.yml:365`; rust template has a `git ls-files` fallback at :310-324), and `upload-pages-artifact` lacks `include-hidden-files: true` (`release.yml:1735-1738` vs rust :947) so dotfiles are dropped from the Pages tarball.\n6. **F6/F7 — steps that pass while doing nothing**: screenshot upload is `if: always()` with default `if-no-files-found: warn` (`release.yml:1263-1271`); desktop checksum-fragment uploads likewise (`desktop-release.yml:492-497,578-583`).\n7. **F8 — PR dry runs get `contents: write` + `attestations: write`** (`desktop-release.yml:161-164`) though attest/upload are disabled for PRs.\n8. **F12/F11/F10 — shell & supply chain**: unpinned `npx --yes secretlint` and diff-only scope vs the rust template's full-tree scan (`scripts/check-secrets.sh:80-84`); `scripts/install.sh:30` uses `set -eu` without `pipefail` (only script in the repo missing it); unquoted `origin/$BASE_REF` at `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh:44,54`.\n9. **Adoptable (b)**: rust template's `cargo-lock` guard job (F14), 3-OS test matrix given we ship macOS/Windows desktop binaries (F15), js template's lychee links workflow (F16), and decoupling `deploy-pages` from the release jobs so the site still updates when publishing fails (F17).\n10. **Upstream (d)**: python template `release.yml` has no workflow-level `permissions:` (F22, drafted) and uses redundant `always() && !cancelled()` at :105,186,517 (F23, drafted).\n\nNotable negatives verified (do not re-investigate): all 21 jobs have `timeout-minutes`, no `continue-on-error` anywhere, top-level `permissions: contents: read` on both workflows, all `|| true` uses in `scripts/` are benign (F21), and every `scripts/*.sh` except `install.sh` sets `set -euo pipefail` — the earlier \"missing strict mode\" signal was a `head -5` artifact."
