[2026-07-20T17:24:09.541Z] [INFO]       "content": "  # issue-804-claude-20260720\". The invariant (CONTRIBUTING.md: every commit\n  # carrying Formal-AI-Session must also carry a Formal-AI-Evidence file that\n  # contains \"formal-ai\" and the exact session id) was only ever enforced at\n  # release time, on main, after merge -- where nothing can be fixed without a\n  # new PR. This job runs the *same* code path over the PR's own commits so a\n  # violating commit is rejected before it can break a release.\n  evidence-check:\n    name: Self-Hosting Evidence Check\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - name: Setup Rust\n        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\n\n      - name: Install rust-script\n        run: bash scripts/install-rust-script.sh\n\n      - name: Validate Formal-AI trailers on this pull request\n        env:\n          GITHUB_BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          base=\"origin/${GITHUB_BASE_REF}\"\n          merge_base=\"$(git merge-base \"$base\" HEAD)\"\n          echo \"Validating commits in ${merge_base}..HEAD\"\n          rust-script scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs --since \"$merge_base\" --until HEAD\n\n  # === DOCKER IMAGE CHECK ===\n  # Issue #808: the Dockerfile was only ever built inside `auto-release` /\n  # `manual-release`, i.e. after the crate had already been published to\n  # crates.io. A broken Dockerfile therefore produced a half-finished release\n  # (crate published, no image, no GitHub Release) and could not be caught\n  # before merge. scripts/verify-docker-runtime.sh, which the image installs as\n  # `verify-formal-ai-dind`, had no caller in CI at all. This job builds the\n  # image without pushing and runs that verifier inside it, so both the build",
