[2026-07-20T17:24:58.886Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The parent agent assigned a read-only investigation (repo `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843`, branch `issue-812-7f9674a82402`) with an explicit constraint stated verbatim: \"Do NOT commit or push anything. Read-only investigation plus writing ONE markdown report.\" The subject: the \"Desktop Release\" workflow fails on `Build macos-x64` and `Build macos-arm64` with `codesign ... Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework: unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework`. Prior analysis of the same defect (\"Defect B\") is in `dev/log/issues/810/pulls/811/analysis.md` (sections 3 and 8), to be read first. Six numbered sub-tasks:\n   1. Read `desktop/package.json` (electron-builder config), `desktop/scripts/*.cjs`, afterPack/afterSign hooks, and how `browser-runtime` gets into `Contents/Resources`.\n   2. Inspect electron-builder / app-builder-lib / @electron/osx-sign sources to find the code path that signs `Contents/Resources/**/Frameworks/*.framework` — `opts.binaries`, `signAsync`, `--deep`/framework enumeration, and any electron-builder `MacPackager` re-sign after the hook returns; with exact file:line references.\n   3. In `run-29752745259.log`, find the ordering: which sign phase emits the failing line, whether `[adhoc-sign-mac]` lines appear at all in THIS run, and what `considered=`/`skipped=` report.\n   4. Explain \"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\" precisely (codesign's layout rule for embedded .framework bundles) and why Chrome for Testing violates it when nested; search online and cite URLs.\n   5. Check whether existing libraries/components solve this (@electron/osx-sign ignore semantics, electron-builder `asarUnpack`, `extraResources` with archives, puppeteer runtime download, `@puppeteer/browsers`); cite URLs.\n   6. Propose ranked, concrete fixes with code/config diff sketches, saying which is structural rather than a workaround.\n   Report destination: `dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis/macos-codesign.md`. Rigor requirement: \"every claim either cites a log line number, a file:line, or a URL. Say plainly what remains unproven.\" Final message must be a 20-line summary of root cause + recommended fix. Additional stated context: the parent agent believed it was \"Established by prior iteration\" that the hook IS invoked, the ignore predicate IS consulted, and osx-sign DOES skip browser-runtime paths — the investigation disproved that this held for the failing run.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - electron-builder 26.15.3 / app-builder-lib `MacPackager.doSign` custom `mac.sign` hook resolution.\n   - `@electron/osx-sign@1.3.3` `signAsync` / `signApplication`, `validateOptsIgnore` array-dropping bug (fixed in 2.x).\n   - `walkAsync` child enumeration, depth-descending sort, per-file codesign invocation, `opts.binaries`.\n   - electron-builder `mac.signIgnore` → compiled into a single `ignore` FUNCTION by `MacTargetHelper.buildSignOptions`.\n   - macOS codesign sealing rules for embedded versioned framework bundles (root must contain only symlinks + `Versions`).\n   - Node `fs.cpSync` `verbatimSymlinks` semantics (default rewrites symlink targets to absolute paths).\n   - Playwright Chrome for Testing runtime copied into `extraResources` → `Contents/Resources/browser-runtime`.\n   - GitHub Actions `workflow_run` healing job that checks out an immutable release TAG rather than main.\n   - Self-hosting metric ratchet gate blocking `Auto Release` (prevents cutting a new tag).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `dev/log/issues/810/pulls/811/analysis.md` — prior analysis; §3 \"Defect B\" and §8 claimed the ignore predicate is consulted and browser-runtime skipped (evidence from PR run 29746221627). Establishes the three candidate fixes (fix ignore path; ship runtime as archive; move runtime out of bundle).\n   - `desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.cjs` (main, current) — custom sign hook. Key parts: `log()` via `fs.writeSync(2, ...)`; `findAppPath`; `isBundledBrowserRuntime(filePath, appPath)`; `signingIgnoreRules(signOptions)` returning a single predicate function with `predicate.stats = {considered, skipped}`; `module.exports = async function adhocSignMac(signOptions)` which requires `MACOS_ADHOC_SIGN === '1'`, calls `signAsync({...signOptions, ignore, identity:'-', identityValidation:false, provisioningProfile:undefined, timestamp:'none', optionsForFile})`, logs `ignore predicate: considered=N skipped=M` in a `finally`, then runs `/usr/bin/codesign --force --timestamp=none --sign -` on the app and `--verify --deep --strict --verbose=2`.\n   - `desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.cjs` at tag `v0.300.0` — pre-fix version: no `fs` require, no logging, and critically `ignore: signingIgnoreRules(signOptions)` at line 129 where `signingIgnoreRules` returns an ARRAY: `return [...upstreamIgnore, (filePath) => isBundledBrowserRuntime(filePath, appPath)];`.\n   - `desktop/package.json` (main) — `extraResources: [{from: \"bin\"...}, {from: \"browser-runtime\", to: \"browser-runtime\", filter: [\"**/*\"]}]`, `mac.hardenedRuntime: true`, `mac.signIgnore: [\"/Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/\"]`, `mac.entitlements`/`entitlementsInherit: build/entitlements.mac.plist`, `asar: true`. At v0.300.0 `signIgnore` is ABSENT.\n   - `desktop/scripts/prepare-resources.mjs` — `copyDirectory()` uses `fs.cpSync(from, to, { recursive: true, verbatimSymlinks: true })` on main (added by 56fa089c for #808); at v0.300.0 line 46 is `fs.cpSync(from, to, { recursive: true });`. Runs `playwright install chromium` then copies `chromium.executablePath()`'s directory to `desktop/browser-runtime`.\n   - `.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml` — build job step `actions/checkout@v6` with `ref: ${{ github.event_name != 'pull_request' && needs.resolve.outputs.tag || '' }}` (line ~173); macOS ad-hoc step runs `npx --no-install electron-builder --mac --publish never -c.mac.notarize=false -c.mac.identity=- -c.mac.sign=./scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.cjs` with env `MACOS_ADHOC_SIGN=1`, `CSC_FOR_PULL_REQUEST=true`, `FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG=1`, `DEBUG=electron-builder,electron-osx-sign*`.\n   - `app-builder-lib@26.15.3/out/macPackager.js:323-334` — `doSign`: `const customSign = await resolveFunction(...)`; logs `customSign ? \"executing custom sign\" : \"signing\"`; `return customSign ? Promise.resolve(customSign(opts, this)) : sign({...})`. No post-hook re-sign of the outer bundle.\n   - `app-builder-lib@26.15.3/out/mac/MacTargetHelper.js:52-120` — `buildSignOptions`: builds `filterRe` from `config.signIgnore` and returns `ignore: (file) => {...}` as a FUNCTION (line 90), plus `binaries` (line 72) and `optionsForFile`.\n   - `@electron/osx-sign@1.3.3/dist/cjs/sign.js:52-55` — `function validateOptsIgnore(ignore) { if (ignore && !(ignore instanceof Array)) { return [ignore]; } }` → arrays silently become `undefined`; used at line 70 in `validateSignOpts`. `signApplication` at 160-270: `shouldIgnoreFilePath`, `walkAsync(getAppContentsPath(opts))`, `if (opts.binaries) children.push(...opts.binaries)`, depth-descending sort, `for (const filePath of [...children, opts.app])` with `debugLog('Skipped... ')` when ignored, final `execFileAsync('codesign', perFileArgs.concat('--entitlements', ..., filePath))`.\n   - `@electron/osx-sign@2.6.0/dist/sign.js:22-26` — fixed: `return Array.isArray(ignore) ? ignore : [ignore];`.\n   - `dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809/2026-07-20-symlink-root-cause.md` — documents that non-verbatim `cpSync` makes framework aliases absolute into `~/.cache/ms-playwright/...`, causing `invalid destination for symbolic link in bundle` on `codesign --verify --deep`.\n   - `dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/ci-logs/run-29752745259.log` key lines: 7156 `ref: v0.300.0`; 7323 `HEAD is now at 78f0800 chore: release v0.300.0`; 8411 `FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG: 1`; 8831 `• executing custom sign file=release/mac/formal-ai Desktop.app ... identityName=-`; 8832 `electron-osx-sign@1.3.3`; 8841 `> Additional binaries: undefined`; 8844/8846/8848 first `Signing...` lines already inside `browser-runtime/Frameworks/Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework/Versions/149.0.7827.55/...` and `Versions/Current/...`; 11760 `Signing... ...Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework` (the bundle itself, signed last because of the depth sort); 11762 `Error executing file`; 11765 `unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework`; arm64 mirror at 13454/16383/16385/16388. ZERO `[adhoc-sign-mac]` lines and ZERO `Skipped...` lines in the whole run.\n   - `dev/log/issues/810/pulls/811/ci-logs/adhoc-sign-mac-29746221627.log` lines 738 and 1481: `[adhoc-sign-mac] ignore predicate: considered=1479 skipped=751` (both mac jobs), and `gh run view 29746221627` shows both macOS jobs `success`.\n   - `dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/ci-logs/run-29751001867.log` — CI/CD Pipeline push on e6510f16: `Auto Release` fails with `Error recording self-hosting release metric: self-hosting ratchet would fall from 32.68% to 18.24% for v0.301.0`.\n   - Created (empty so far): directory `dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis/`. The report file `macos-codesign.md` has NOT been written yet.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Initial assumption (inherited from the parent agent's brief) that the hook ran and the ignore predicate was consulted in run 29752745259: disproved by `grep -c \"adhoc-sign-mac\"` → 6 hits, all command echoes, and 0 `Skipped...` lines. Fixed the interpretation by reading the checkout step: the job builds tag `v0.300.0`, whose code predates the instrumentation and the fixes.\n   - Prior analysis' claim that electron-builder forwards `mac.signIgnore` \"as an array\": corrected — `MacTargetHelper.buildSignOptions` passes `ignore` as a function (MacTargetHelper.js:90); it is OUR pre-fix hook that converted it into an array, which `validateOptsIgnore` then discarded (dropping electron-builder's own kext/PlugIns/puppeteer rules too).\n   - `unpkg` 404s for `app-builder-lib/out/macPackagerHelper.js` and for `@electron/osx-sign@2.6.0/dist/cjs/sign.js`: resolved by reading `require` paths in macPackager.js (`./mac/MacTargetHelper`) and by fetching `@electron/osx-sign@2.6.0/dist/sign.js`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Root cause established: the Desktop Release \"healing\" run checks out release tag v0.300.0 (created 2026-07-19T18:05Z), which predates every packaging fix landed on main on 2026-07-20 (a6f0f040 function-form ignore, 56fa089c `verbatimSymlinks: true`, 39fdef91 `mac.signIgnore`, 1b1586bb instrumentation). At that tag the hook hands `@electron/osx-sign@1.3.3` an ARRAY `ignore`, which `validateOptsIgnore` silently converts to `undefined`, so every ignore rule (ours and electron-builder's) is discarded; osx-sign therefore walks into `Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/...` and finally codesigns the Chrome for Testing framework bundle itself (log 11760), which fails the embedded-framework sealing rule (log 11765). The fixed code is proven to work (PR run 29746221627 succeeded with `considered=1479 skipped=751`). Secondary structural problem: `Auto Release` now fails on the self-hosting ratchet, so no new tag can be cut, so the desktop release will rebuild the broken tag forever — a deadlock of the same class as Defect A. Unproven items to state plainly: whether the framework could ever be signed successfully even with correct relative symlinks (never tested — the fixed run skips it), and the exact internal reason codesign classifies the copied framework root as \"unsealed\" (inferred from the absolute-symlink evidence in the #808 note plus Apple forum guidance, not directly observed via a directory listing from CI).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843 (repo li