[2026-07-20T17:25:48.644Z] [INFO]         "text": "Report written to `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis/macos-codesign.md`. No commits, no pushes (the pre-existing dirty files in `git status` are not mine).\n\n1. Root cause is not a signing bug that still needs diagnosing — the failing run builds the wrong code.\n2. Run 29752745259 is a `workflow_run` \"healing\" build; every job checks out `ref: v0.300.0` (log:7156, :11854 → `HEAD is now at 78f0800`, :7323).\n3. Tag `v0.300.0` (2026-07-19) predates all four packaging fixes landed on `main` on 2026-07-20: `a6f0f040` (function-form ignore), `56fa089c` (`verbatimSymlinks: true`), `39fdef91` (`mac.signIgnore`), `1b1586bb` (instrumentation).\n4. At that tag the hook passes `ignore` as an **array** to `@electron/osx-sign@1.3.3`.\n5. `validateOptsIgnore` (`sign.js:52-56`) has no `return ignore` for the array branch, so an array yields `undefined` and every rule is discarded — ours *and* electron-builder's kext/PlugIns/puppeteer rules from `MacTargetHelper.js:90-107`.\n6. Proof in the log: 0 occurrences of `Skipped`, and 0 `[adhoc-sign-mac]` lines despite `FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG: 1` (:8411).\n7. So osx-sign's `walkAsync` (`sign.js:172`) descends into `Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/…` (:8844, :8846).\n8. Children are sorted deepest-first (`sign.js:183-186`), so the framework *bundle itself* is signed last, at :11760 — that is the invocation that fails (:11762, :11765).\n9. `opts.binaries` is not involved: `> Additional binaries: undefined` (:8841).\n10. There is no second signer: `macPackager.js:323-334` returns the custom hook's promise and never re-signs; the \"electron-builder re-signs afterwards\" hypothesis is disproved by source.\n11. \"Unsealed contents in the root of an embedded framework\" = a versioned `.framework` may contain only `Versions/` plus symlinks into `Versions/Current` at its root (Apple forums thread 93914).\n12. At `v0.300.0` those root aliases are absolute paths into `~/.cache/ms-playwright` because `cpSync` defaults to `verbatimSymlinks: false` — corroborated by `dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809/2026-07-20-symlink-root-cause.md`.\n13. The fixed code is proven green: PR run 29746221627 logs `considered=1479 skipped=751` and both macOS jobs succeeded.\n14. Recommended fix F1 (mandatory, first): cut a new tag. Nothing in `desktop/` needs to change for the red build to clear.\n15. F1 is blocked by a second deadlock: `Auto Release` fails with `self-hosting ratchet would fall from 32.68% to 18.24% for v0.301.0` (`run-29751001867.log:1418`), so no newer tag can exist and Desktop Release will rebuild `v0.300.0` forever.\n16. F2 (structural packaging fix): ship `browser-runtime` as a single `.zip` in `extraResources` and expand on first run — a blob is unwalkable, so codesign can never reach a foreign framework.\n17. F3 (strongest, bigger behaviour change): don't bundle a browser; fetch via `@puppeteer/browsers` into `app.getPath('userData')`.\n18. F4 (hardening): keep the function-form ignore and add `\"overrides\": {\"@electron/osx-sign\": \"^2.6.0\"}` — v2 fixed the array bug (`2.6.0/dist/sign.js:22-26`).\n19. F5 (recurrence): add a `push: branches: [main]` macOS dry run, or make `desktop-release-resolve.sh` refuse to heal a tag lacking the packaging contract.\n20. Unproven and stated as such in the report: whether the Chrome framework could ever be re-signed successfully (never tested — green runs skip it), the exact codesign predicate behind the message (inferred, no CI directory listing), and osx-sign v2 compatibility with app-builder-lib 26."
