[2026-07-20T17:44:45.088Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   One genuine user message directed solving GitHub issue https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/812 (\"Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all\") in `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843`, on branch `issue-812-7f9674a82402`, updating existing PR https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/813.\n\n   Explicit user requirements:\n   - \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813 folder.\"\n   - \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   - \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   - \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   - \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n\n   Environment/guideline constraints: push ONLY to `issue-812-7f9674a82402`; PR 813 already exists (update, don't create); run local CI checks before pushing; commit atomic steps; `gh pr ready 813` when finished; save large logs to files; read files >1500 lines in chunks; keep debug/test scripts in `./examples` and/or `./experiments`.\n\n   Issue-body requirements: compare the **full file tree** against `link-foundation/{rust,js,python}-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`; report the same defect upstream in the templates where present; follow `https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`; \"plan and execute everything in this single pull request … until it is each and every requirement fully addressed\".\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - GitHub Actions: `release.yml` (\"CI/CD Pipeline\"), `desktop-release.yml` (\"Desktop Release\"), `workflow_run` healing builds, job `needs:`/`if:`/`timeout-minutes`, `::warning` annotations\n   - `rust-script` standalone scripts in `scripts/*.rs`, included into tests via `#[path = \"../../../scripts/x.rs\"] mod`\n   - Links Notation (`.lino`) ledger, `links_notation::parse_lino`\n   - Self-hosting metric: `Formal-AI-Session`/`Formal-AI-Evidence` trailers, basis-point arithmetic, trailing-window weighted ratchet\n   - `EvidencePolicy::{Strict, Lenient}` (issue #810 precedent) and the new `RatchetPolicy::{Enforce, Report}`\n   - `METRIC_VERSION` measurement-epoch versioning of ledger rows\n   - Differential (branch-vs-base) gating to avoid non-actionable deadlocks\n   - electron-builder / `@electron/osx-sign` ad-hoc codesigning; `validateOptsIgnore` array bug in v1.3.3\n   - `clippy::pedantic`/`nursery` lints: `format_collect`, `format_push_string`, `option_if_let_else`, `match_single_binding`\n   - POSIX `sh` vs bash: `pipefail` is not POSIX\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs`** — the primary file. Already had (pre-compaction): module doc update, `METRIC_VERSION: u64 = 2`, `CAPTURED_ARTIFACT_EXTENSIONS = &[\"log\",\"jsonl\",\"diff\",\"patch\",\"stderr\",\"stdout\"]`, `LOCKFILE_NAMES` (Cargo.lock, bun.lock, package-lock.json, yarn.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml, poetry.lock, uv.lock), `ReleaseRow.metric_version`, `is_non_authored_path()`, its use in `changed_lines_for_commit`, `RatchetPolicy`, `record_release_with_policy`, `ratchet_regression`, epoch-filtered `rows`, `parse_release_row` backward-compatible epoch parsing.\n\n     New this session:\n     ```rust\n     fn append_release_row(ledger: &Path, row: &ReleaseRow) -> Result<(), String> {\n         let mut file = OpenOptions::new().append(true).open(ledger)\n             .map_err(|error| format!(\"could not append {}: {error}\", ledger.display()))?;\n         let fields = [\n             (\"metric_version\", row.metric_version.to_string()),\n             (\"tag\", row.tag.clone()),\n             (\"since\", row.since.clone()),\n             (\"until\", row.until.clone()),\n             (\"self_authored_lines\", row.self_authored_lines.to_string()),\n             (\"changed_lines\", row.changed_lines.to_string()),\n             (\"self_authored_commits\", row.self_authored_commits.to_string()),\n             (\"commits\", row.commits.to_string()),\n             (\"percentage_basis_points\", row.percentage_basis_points.to_string()),\n             (\"trailing_window\", row.trailing_window.to_string()),\n             (\"trailing_percentage_basis_points\", row.trailing_percentage_basis_points.to_string()),\n         ];\n         let mut record = String::from(\"  release\\n\");\n         for (key, value) in &fields {\n             record.push_str(\"    \"); record.push_str(key); record.push_str(\" \\\"\");\n             record.push_str(value); record.push_str(\"\\\"\\n\");\n         }\n         write!(file, \"{record}\")\n             .map_err(|error| format!(\"could not append {}: {error}\", ledger.display()))\n     }\n     ```\n     ```rust\n     /// The trailing share a release cut at `until` would record. [...]\n     pub fn project_trailing_basis_points(repo: &Path, ledger: &Path, since: &str,\n         until: &str, trailing_window: usize) -> Result<u64, String> { ... }\n\n     /// Whether merging `head` would lower the share the next release records.\n     /// The comparison is *differential* [...] A no-op pull request is always neutral.\n     pub fn ratchet_check(repo: &Path, ledger: &Path, base: &str, head: &str,\n         trailing_window: usize) -> Result<Option<String>, String> {\n         let Some(since) = read_release_rows(ledger)?.last().map(|row| row.tag.clone()) else {\n             return Ok(None);\n         };\n         // A checkout without tags (shallow clone, fork without `fetch-tags`) cannot\n         // measure the release range. Skip loudly rather than fail [...]\n         if git(repo, &[\"rev-parse\",\"--verify\",\"--quiet\",&format!(\"{since}^{{commit}}\")]).is_err() {\n             eprintln!(\"warning: skipping ratchet check: {since} is not present in this checkout\");\n             return Ok(None);\n         }\n         let baseline = project_trailing_basis_points(repo, ledger, &since, base, trailing_window)?;\n         let candidate = project_trailing_basis_points(repo, ledger, &since, head, trailing_window)?;\n         if candidate >= baseline { return Ok(None); }\n         Ok(Some(format!(\"merging this branch would lower the projected self-hosting share of \\\n             the next release from {} to {}; record Formal-AI-Session and Formal-AI-Evidence \\\n             trailers on the commits that Formal AI authored, or split unattributed work out of \\\n             this branch\", format_percentage(baseline), format_percentage(candidate))))\n     }\n     ```\n     `Options` now has `since: Option<String>` and `check_ratchet: Option<String>`; `run()` handles `--check-ratchet` first (`if let Some(regression) = ratchet_check(...)? { return Err(regression) }` then prints \"self-hosting ratchet holds against {base}\"), and the record path uses `record_release_with_policy(..., RatchetPolicy::Report)`. `optional_number` uses `let Ok(raw) = value(key) else { return Ok(None) };`.\n\n   - **`scripts/version-and-commit.rs`** (~line 522) — release call site:\n     ```rust\n     // `Report`, not `Enforce`: by the time a release runs, every commit in the\n     // range is immutable history on `main`, so a hard failure here can only\n     // deadlock the release (issue #812). The ratchet is enforced at the\n     // pull-request gate instead — see `self_hosting_metric::RatchetPolicy`.\n     let row = self_hosting_metric::record_release_with_policy(\n         &repo, &ledger, &tag, &since, \"HEAD\", 3,\n         self_hosting_metric::RatchetPolicy::Report,\n     )?;\n     ```\n\n   - **`.github/workflows/release.yml`** — three changes:\n     (a) new step in `evidence-check` after the trailer validation:\n     ```yaml\n     - name: Check the self-hosting ratchet against the merge base\n       env:\n         GITHUB_BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref }}\n       run: |\n         set -euo pipefail\n         base=\"origin/${GITHUB_BASE_REF}\"\n         rust-script scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs --check-ratchet \"$base\" --until HEAD\n     ```\n     (b) `upload-pages-artifact@v5` gained `include-hidden-files: true`;\n     (c) \"Upload generated /download screenshots\" lost `if: always()` and gained `if-no-files-found: error`.\n     File is now ~1824+ lines.\n\n   - **`data/meta/self-hosting-ledger.lino`** — header gained (2-space indent, ignored by the row parser):\n     ```\n     current_metric_version \"2\"\n     metric_version_1 \"every changed line, including captured artifacts\"\n     metric_version_2 \"issue #812: lockfiles and captured artifacts (*.log, *.jsonl, *.diff, *.patch, *.stderr, *.stdout) excluded from both numerator and denominator\"\n     comparable_rows \"only rows sharing a metric_version\"\n     ```\n\n   - **`tests/unit/specification/self_hosting_metric.rs`** — now 8 tests. Four added: `captured_artifacts_and_lockfiles_do_not_move_the_metric`, `rows_from_an_older_measurement_epoch_are_never_compared`, `a_falling_ratchet_reports_at_release_time_instead_of_blocking_it`, `the_pull_request_gate_only_judges_the_branchs_own_delta`. `release_pipeline_and_ledger_remain_pinned_to_the_metric` gained assertions on `workflow.contains(\"--check-ratchet\")`, `version_script.contains(\"RatchetPolicy::Report\")`, `ledger.contains(\"current_metric_version \\\"2\\\"\")`.\n\n   - **`dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis.md`** (created, ~250 lines) — the commit's evidence file. Contains session id `issue-812-claude-20260720` and \"formal-ai\". Sections: evidence inventory, timeline, R1–R9 requirement table, Defect A (two root causes + fix + verification), Defect B summary, template-sweep false negatives table, upstream reports, debug output.\n\n   - **`scripts/install.sh`** — reverted a bad `set -euo pipefail` change back to `set -eu` with an explanatory comment (shebang is `#!/usr/bin/env sh`; `pipefail` breaks dash, i.e. `curl | sh` on Debian/Ubuntu).\n\n   - **`scripts/check-file-size.rs`** — MOST RECENT EDIT, INCOMPLETE. Added const before `EXCLUDE_PATTERNS`:\n     ```rust\n     /// Issue #812: the size gate covered no CI definition at all, so\n     /// `.github/workflows/release.yml` reached 1824 lines -- past the 1500-line\n     /// ceiling the js pipeline template applies to its own workflows -- with CI\n     /// green throughout. [...] The cap is deliberately set above today's worst\n     /// file rather than below it: a hard failure would block every unrelated pull\n     /// request until `release.yml` is split [...]\n     const WORKFLOW_YAML_LIMIT: FileLimit = FileLimit {\n         extension: \"yml\", max_lines: 2_000, warn_lines: 1_500,\n         label: \"GitHub Actions workflow\",\n     };\n     ```\n     Existing relevant code: `FILE_LIMITS` (rs 1000/900, lino 1500/1400), `WORKER_JS_LIMIT`, `EXCLUDE_PATH_FRAGMENTS = &[\"data/cache/wikidata/\", \"dev/log/\"]`, `is_worker_js_path()`, and:\n     ```rust\n     fn file_limit(path: &Path) -> Option<&'static FileLimit> {\n         if is_worker_js_path(path) { return Some(&WORKER_JS_LIMIT); }\n         let ext = path.extension().and_then(|ext| ext.to_str())?;\n         FILE_LIMITS.iter().find(|limit| limit.extension == ext)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`experiments/self_hosting_ratchet_replay/replay.py`** — standalone Python reimplementation of the metric (per-commit attribution + reason + subject, sorted by line count).\n\n   - **`dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis/macos-codesign.md`** and **`.../template-sweep.md`** — subagent reports, committed.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n   - Ugly escaped multi-line format string in `append_release_row` → rewrote as a `fields` array + `push_str` loop.\n   - `--check-ratchet` against `/tmp/ledger-probe.lino` failed with `fatal: ambiguous argument 'v0.301.0..origin/main'` because the probe ledger names a tag that doesn't exist → added the `git rev-parse --verify --quiet` guard so a missing tag warns and skips instead of turning red.\n   - Test `a_falling_ratchet_reports_at_release_time_instead_of_blocking_it` failed: `record_release(..., \"v1.1.0\", ...)` errored because tag `v1.1.0` was never created in the fixture → added `git(&repo, &[\"tag\", \"v1.1.0\"]);` after the first row is recorded.\n   - `cargo fmt --check` diffs → ran `cargo fmt --all`.\n   - Three clippy pedantic warnings I introduced → fixed: `format_collect`/`format_push_string` (plain `push_str` chain), `option_if_let_else` in `optional_number` (let-else), `match_single_binding` + `option_if_let_else` in `run()` (`if let Some(...) { return Err(...) }`).\n   - **Self-caught factual error in analysis.md**: I had written \"v0.300.0's recorded 69.56% becomes 5.39% once artifacts are excluded.\" Measured it: it actually becomes **77.41% (18662/24108)**. Rewrote the section to show the metric distorted in BOTH directions (v0.299.0..v0.300.0: 69.56% → 77.41%; v0.300.0..main: 18.24% → 4.36%).\n   - **Self-caught wrong bucket numbers**: recomputed exactly — total 636,240; `.log` 550,531 (86.53%); `.diff` 41,792 (6.57%); `.lino` 14,713; `.rs` 13,188; `.jsonl` 7,010 (1.10%); `.md` 3,545; captured total **599,340 (94.20%)**; remaining 36,900 (metric reports 36,896 — 4 lines of lockfile churn).\n   - **Self-caught bad fix**: changing `scripts/install.sh` to `set -euo pipefail` would break `curl | sh` under dash → reverted to `set -eu` with a documenting comment.\n   - **Self-caught false finding from the subagent (F13)**: `FILE_SIZE_WARNING_BASE` empty is NOT a bug — `growing_paths_since(\"\")` returns `None`, which falls through to `print_warnings(&result.warnings)` (all warnings). Correct degradation already exists.\n   - No user feedback or corrections were received at any point (only one user message exists).\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n\n   **Defect A — `Auto Release` deadlocked (run 29751001867, log line 23918: `self-hosting ratchet would fall from 32.68% to 18.24% for v0.301.0`).** Two independent root causes, both fixed and verified:\n   1. *Denominator measured log volume*: 599,340 of 636,240 lines (94.20%) in `v0.300.0..main` were captured CI transcripts that the repo requires each iteration to commit. Fix: `is_non_authored_path` excludes captured artifacts + lockfiles symmetrically; `METRIC_VERSION = 2` starts a new comparison epoch so no history is rewritten and epochs are never averaged.\n   2. *Gate ran where nobody could act*: enforcement sat in `record_release` on `main` after commits were immutable, and cutting a tag (the only way to move the range) was what it blocked — third outage of this shape (#796, #810, #812). Fix: `RatchetPolicy::Report` at release time (append row + `::warning`), `RatchetPolicy::Enforce` at the PR gate via `--check-ratchet`, made differential so a pre-existing regression on main can't fail unrelated PRs.\n\n   Verified: the exact failing command now exits 0 → `4.36% (1608/36896 changed lines; 10/119 commits)`. 8 unit tests pass, clippy clean, fmt clean.\n\n   **Defect B — `Desktop Release` macOS codesign (run 29752745259)**: subagent proved it is a `workflow_run` **healing build of tag v0.300.0** (log 7156, 11854, 7323) which predates all four packaging fixes (`a6f0f040`, `56fa089c`, `39fdef91`, `1b1586bb`). At that tag, `ignore` is passed as an array, and `@electron/osx-sign@1.3.3`'s `validateOptsIgnore` (`sign.js:52-56`) has no `return ignore` for arrays, so ALL ignore rules are discarded (proof: 0 `Skipped` and 0 `[adhoc-sign-mac]` lines despite `FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG: 1` at log 8411). `walkAsync` then descends into browser-runtime and signs the framework last (log 11760 → 11765). Fixed code is proven green (PR run 29746221627: `considered=1479 skipped=751`). **B needs no `desktop/` change — it needs a newer tag, which Defect A's fix unblocks.** Disproved hypotheses recorded so nobody re-investigates: `opts.binaries` not involved; electron-builder does not re-sign (`macPackager.js:323-334`). Verified myself that F4's first half (single-function `ignore` predicate) is ALREADY on main in `desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.cjs`; only the unverified `overrides: {\"@electron/osx-sign\": \"^2.6.0\"}` pin remains.\n\n   **Template sweep** produced F1–F23. Key: F3 (`auto-release` needs only `[lint, test, build]`, so e2e/secrets-scan/docker-build can be red while publishing), F1 (no workflow-YAML/`.md` size coverage; release.yml 1824 lines), F2 (`simulate-fresh-merge.sh` unused in desktop-release.yml), F4 (`finalize` uses `always()`, clobbers SHA256SUMS on cancel), F5/F6/F7 (silent no-ops), F12 (unpinned `npx --yes secretlint`), F10 (install.sh — determined to be a non-issue). Plus one found outside the sweep: `cargo clippy` runs without `-D warnings` at `release.yml:355`.\n\n   **Committed & pushed**: `e80d47ee` \"fix(ci): stop the self-hosting ratchet from deadlocking every release\" with the required trailers; evidence gate verified passing (`99.94% (5059/5062 changed lines; 1/2 commits)`).\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/812 / Your prepared 