[2026-07-20T18:09:41.259Z] [INFO]           " | R476 | Record a self-hosting row for every release as committed Links Notation data. | `scripts/version-and-commit.rs` records the new tag's row in `data/meta/self-hosting-ledger.lino` before the release commit and stages it with the version artifacts. The initial `v0.296.0` row truthfully records 0%. |",
[2026-07-20T18:09:41.259Z] [INFO]           " | R477 | Include the recorded share in every GitHub release body. | Both automatic and manual paths in `.github/workflows/release.yml` pass the ledger to `scripts/create-github-release.rs`, which appends the exact tagged row under `## Self-hosting`. |",
[2026-07-20T18:09:41.259Z] [INFO]           "-| R478 | Enforce a monotonic non-decreasing trailing-window ratchet while accepting an honest 0% starting point. | `record_release` computes a changed-line-weighted three-release share, rejects a decrease, and treats an empty history as 0%; the fixture test covers both first-row acceptance and regression rejection. |",
[2026-07-20T18:09:41.259Z] [INFO]           "+| R478 | Enforce a monotonic non-decreasing trailing-window ratchet while accepting an honest 0% starting point. | `record_release` computes a changed-line-weighted three-release share and treats an empty history as 0%. Issue #812 moved *where* the decrease is rejected: at release time the ratchet is `RatchetPolicy::Report` (record the row, emit a `::warning`), because by then every contributing commit is immutable history on `main` and the only way to move the measured range forward — cutting a tag — is what a hard failure blocks. Enforcement is `RatchetPolicy::Enforce` at the pull-request gate (`--check-ratchet`), where commits can still be amended, and is differential: it compares the share projected *with* the branch against the one projected for the base alone, so a regression already on `main` cannot fail unrelated pull requests. Covered by `a_falling_ratchet_reports_at_release_time_instead_of_blocking_it` and `the_pull_request_gate_only_judges_the_branchs_own_delta`. |",
[2026-07-20T18:09:41.259Z] [INFO]           " | R479 | Document attribution, preserve issue/PR/research and Formal AI replay evidence, and pin pipeline integration with a specification test. | Implemented by `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `docs/case-studies/issue-657/`, and `release_pipeline_and_ledger_remain_pinned_to_the_metric`. |",
[2026-07-20T18:09:41.259Z] [INFO]           "+| R480 | A change to how the share is measured must start a new comparison epoch instead of silently invalidating recorded history. | Implemented by `METRIC_VERSION` in `scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs`: every ledger row carries the version that produced it, `rows` filters to the current epoch, and `parse_release_row` treats a row without the field as epoch 1. Rows from different epochs are never averaged or compared. The ledger header documents what each epoch measures. Covered by `rows_from_an_older_measurement_epoch_are_never_compared`. |",
[2026-07-20T18:09:41.259Z] [INFO]           " ",
