[2026-07-20T18:10:16.376Z] [INFO]       "content": "  resolve:\n    name: Resolve target release\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n    # For workflow_run, continue after ANY completed main-branch pipeline except\n    # cancelled/skipped runs (issue #479). We intentionally do NOT gate on\n    # conclusion == 'success': the auto-release publishes the GitHub release in an\n    # EARLY pipeline job, so a LATER job failing (e.g. the E2E Pages probe timing\n    # out) still leaves a real, asset-less release that desktop assets must heal.\n    # Gating on full-pipeline green meant one unrelated late failure suppressed\n    # every desktop build -> \"Not available in latest release\". The actual\n    # decision to build is delegated to scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh, whose\n    # idempotency guard skips when the resolved release already carries desktop\n    # assets, so running on a non-success conclusion is safe and self-healing.\n    # Pull requests resolve nothing: there is no release to heal and no tag to\n    # check out. The job is skipped and `build` admits the skipped dependency\n    # explicitly, so the packaging matrix still runs against the PR head.\n    if: >-\n      github.event_name != 'pull_request' &&\n      (github.event_name != 'workflow_run' ||\n      (github.event.workflow_run.head_branch == 'main' &&\n       github.event.workflow_run.conclusion != 'cancelled' &&\n       github.event.workflow_run.conclusion != 'skipped'))\n    outputs:\n      tag: ${{ steps.pick.outputs.tag }}\n      should_build: ${{ steps.pick.outputs.should_build }}\n    steps:\n      # Check out the repo so the resolve logic lives in a unit-tested script\n      # (scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh) instead of being inlined here. The\n      # script only needs to *exist*; it queries the GitHub API for everything\n      # else, so checking out the default ref is sufficient.\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n\n      - name: Resolve tag and whether desktop assets are needed\n        id: pick\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}\n          INPUT_TAG: ${{ github.event.inputs.tag }}\n          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }}\n          REPO: ${{ github.repository }}\n          WORKFLOW_RUN_HEAD_SHA: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.head_sha }}\n        # Issue #479: the automated release tags a CHILD \"chore: release vX.Y.Z\"\n        # commit whose first parent is the completed CI head SHA, so matching the\n        # tag to the head SHA directly always failed and desktop assets were\n        # never built. desktop-release-resolve.sh resolves the latest release\n        # instead (with a defensive exact-SHA tier and an idempotency guard) and\n        # emits verbose ::group:: diagnostics for future debugging.\n        run: bash scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh\n\n  build:\n    name: Build ${{ matrix.label }}\n    needs: resolve",
