[2026-07-20T18:24:05.864Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   One genuine user message directed solving GitHub issue https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/812 (\"Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all\") in `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843`, on branch `issue-812-7f9674a82402`, updating existing PR https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/813.\n\n   Explicit user requirements (verbatim intent):\n   - \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813 folder.\"\n   - \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   - \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   - \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   - \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n\n   Environment/guideline constraints: push ONLY to `issue-812-7f9674a82402`; PR 813 already exists (update via `gh pr edit`, don't create); run local CI checks before pushing; commit atomic steps; `gh pr ready 813` when finished; save large logs to files; read files >1500 lines in chunks; keep debug/test scripts in `./examples` and/or `./experiments`.\n\n   Issue-body requirements: compare the full file tree against `link-foundation/{rust,js,python}-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`; report the same defect upstream in the templates where present; follow `https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`; \"plan and execute everything in this single pull request … until it is each and every requirement fully addressed\".\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - GitHub Actions: `needs:`/`if:`/`timeout-minutes`, `!cancelled()` vs `always()`, `workflow_run` healing builds, `::warning`/`::notice`/`::error` annotations, `needs.<job>.result` values (success/failure/cancelled/skipped)\n   - GitHub expression truthiness: numeric `0` is falsy, so `${{ cond && 0 || 1 }}` is wrong; must use quoted `'0'`/`'1'`\n   - `rust-script` standalone scripts in `scripts/*.rs`, included into tests via `#[path = \"../../../scripts/x.rs\"] mod`\n   - actionlint 1.7.7 (type-checks `needs`/`steps`/`env` contexts, embeds shellcheck over `run:` blocks); `.github/actionlint.yaml` `self-hosted-runner.labels`\n   - shellcheck 0.10.0: SC2066 (quoted single-word for-loop), SC2012 (`ls` parsing), SC2046/SC2010 (`$(ls | grep)`), SC2086 (unquoted expansion), SC2164, SC2034, SC2064\n   - Self-hosting metric: `Formal-AI-Session`/`Formal-AI-Evidence` trailers, basis-point arithmetic, trailing-window weighted ratchet, `RatchetPolicy::{Enforce, Report}`, `METRIC_VERSION` measurement epochs, differential (branch-vs-base) gating\n   - `clippy::pedantic`/`nursery` with `[lints.clippy] all/pedantic/nursery = \"warn\"` — requires `-D warnings` at the CLI to actually gate\n   - electron-builder / `@electron/osx-sign` ad-hoc codesigning; `validateOptsIgnore` array bug in v1.3.3\n   - POSIX `sh` vs bash: `pipefail` is not POSIX (breaks `curl | sh` under dash)\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`scripts/check-file-size.rs`** — COMPLETED this session. The `.git` substring exclusion made every workflow invisible to the size gate.\n     ```rust\n     /// Issue #812: `EXCLUDE_PATTERNS` are directory *names*, so they are matched per\n     /// path component. A substring test hid every workflow from the gate --\n     /// `.github/workflows/release.yml` contains `.git` -- and would likewise skip\n     /// any path with `target` or `node_modules` inside a longer segment.\n     fn should_exclude(path: &Path) -> bool {\n         let path_str = normalized_path(path);\n         path_str\n             .split('/')\n             .any(|component| EXCLUDE_PATTERNS.contains(&component))\n             || EXCLUDE_PATH_FRAGMENTS\n                 .iter()\n                 .any(|fragment| path_str.contains(fragment))\n     }\n     ```\n     ```rust\n     /// Only workflows this repository owns are measured. `docs/case-studies/**`\n     /// holds verbatim copies of other projects' pipelines as evidence; reformatting\n     /// them to fit our ceiling would destroy the thing they document.\n     fn is_workflow_yaml_path(path: &Path) -> bool {\n         let path_str = normalized_path(path);\n         let has_yaml_extension = path\n             .extension()\n             .and_then(|extension| extension.to_str())\n             .is_some_and(|extension| {\n                 extension.eq_ignore_ascii_case(\"yml\") || extension.eq_ignore_ascii_case(\"yaml\")\n             });\n         has_yaml_extension && (path_str.starts_with(\".github/\") || path_str.contains(\"/.github/\"))\n     }\n\n     fn file_limit(path: &Path) -> Option<&'static FileLimit> {\n         if is_worker_js_path(path) { return Some(&WORKER_JS_LIMIT); }\n         if is_workflow_yaml_path(path) { return Some(&WORKFLOW_YAML_LIMIT); }\n         let ext = path.extension().and_then(|ext| ext.to_str())?;\n         FILE_LIMITS.iter().find(|limit| limit.extension == ext)\n     }\n     ```\n     `WORKFLOW_YAML_LIMIT` = `{extension: \"yml\", max_lines: 2_000, warn_lines: 1_500, label: \"GitHub Actions workflow\"}` (cap deliberately above today's worst file so it warns rather than blocks unrelated PRs). Intro string now reads \"…Rust, Links Notation, worker JavaScript, and GitHub Actions workflow files…\". Two new tests added: `check_directory_measures_github_workflows` and `check_directory_does_not_measure_quoted_case_study_workflows` (uses `docs/case-studies/issue-561/template-comparison/js/release.yml`). Verified: 14 tests pass; release.yml at 1824 lines emits a warning, script exits 0.\n\n   - **`.github/workflows/release.yml`** — five changes this session:\n     (a) Clippy now gates:\n     ```yaml\n     # `-D warnings` is required, not optional: every lint in `[lints.clippy]`\n     # of Cargo.toml is set to `warn`, so without it clippy printed findings\n     # and still exited 0 -- a green check over unreviewed lint debt\n     # (issue #812). The tree is clippy-clean at the time this was added, so\n     # this promotes existing behaviour rather than introducing new failures.\n     - name: Run Clippy\n       run: cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\n     ```\n     (b) Two new lint steps before \"Check formatting\":\n     ```yaml\n     - name: Lint GitHub Actions workflows\n       env:\n         ACTIONLINT_VERSION: 1.7.7\n       run: |\n         set -euo pipefail\n         curl -fsSL \\\n           \"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/releases/download/v${ACTIONLINT_VERSION}/actionlint_${ACTIONLINT_VERSION}_linux_amd64.tar.gz\" \\\n           | tar xz -C /tmp actionlint\n         /tmp/actionlint -color\n\n     - name: Lint shell scripts\n       run: |\n         set -euo pipefail\n         mapfile -t scripts < <(\n           git ls-files '*.sh' \\\n             | grep -v -e '^experiments/' -e '^dev/log/' -e '^docs/case-studies/'\n         )\n         if [ ${#scripts[@]} -eq 0 ]; then\n           echo \"::error::No shell scripts matched; the lint selector is broken\" >&2\n           exit 1\n         fi\n         printf 'Linting %s shell script(s)\\n' \"${#scripts[@]}\"\n         shellcheck --severity=warning \"${scripts[@]}\"\n     ```\n     (c) Release gates (both `auto-release` and `manual-release`):\n     ```yaml\n     needs: [lint, test, build, secrets-scan, test-e2e-local, test-agent-cli-e2e]\n     if: |\n       !cancelled() &&\n       github.event_name == 'push' &&\n       github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' &&\n       needs.build.result == 'success' &&\n       needs.secrets-scan.result != 'failure' &&\n       needs.test-e2e-local.result != 'failure' &&\n       needs.test-agent-cli-e2e.result != 'failure'\n     ```\n     (d) \"Run desktop library tests\" rewritten from `node --test $(ls desktop/scripts/*.test.mjs | grep -v '/web-tools.test.mjs)` to an explicit `shopt -s nullglob` + array build + empty-list `::error` guard + `node --test \"${tests[@]}\"`.\n     (e) `echo \"$HOME/.bun/bin\" >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"` (was unquoted).\n     Also carried over uncommitted from before compaction: `include-hidden-files: true` on `upload-pages-artifact`, and screenshot upload changed from `if: always()` to `if-no-files-found: error`.\n\n   - **`.github/actionlint.yaml`** — NEW:\n     ```yaml\n     self-hosted-runner:\n       labels:\n         - macos-15-intel\n         - windows-11-arm\n     ```\n     (Both are real 2025 GitHub-hosted runners newer than actionlint 1.7.7's baked-in label list.)\n\n   - **`.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml`** — four changes:\n     (a) `finalize` job: `always()` → `!cancelled()` with a comment explaining that `gh release upload --clobber` under `always()` lets a cancelled run overwrite a complete `SHA256SUMS.txt` with a partial one.\n     (b) `build` and `vscode` jobs gained `fetch-depth: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && '0' || '1' }}` plus a \"Simulate fresh merge with base branch (PR only)\" step running `bash scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` with `BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref }}`.\n     (c) SC2066 fix: `dmgs=(\"release/formal-ai-desktop-macos-${ARCH}-${VERSION}.dmg\")` then `for dmg in \"${dmgs[@]}\"; do`.\n     (d) SC2012 fix in vscode packaging: `shopt -s nullglob; vsix_files=(formal-ai-vscode-*.vsix); vsix=\"${vsix_files[0]:-}\"`.\n\n   - **`scripts/check-secrets.sh`** — secretlint pinned:\n     ```bash\n     SECRETLINT_VERSION=\"${SECRETLINT_VERSION:-13.0.2}\"\n     debug \"secretlint ${SECRETLINT_VERSION}\"\n     printf '%s\\0' \"${files[@]}\" |\n       xargs -0 npx --yes \\\n         -p \"secretlint@${SECRETLINT_VERSION}\" \\\n         -p \"@secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend@${SECRETLINT_VERSION}\" \\\n         secretlint\n     ```\n\n   - **`scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh`** — `BEHIND_COUNT=$(git rev-list --count \"HEAD..origin/$BASE_REF\")` and `if git merge \"origin/$BASE_REF\" --no-edit; then`; header note changed from \"Adopted verbatim\" to explain the quoting divergence from upstream.\n\n   - **`scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh`** — healing-build notice added inside `emit_outputs()`:\n     ```bash\n     if [ \"$should_build\" = \"true\" ] && [ -n \"$tag\" ]; then\n       head_sha=\"$(gh api \"repos/${REPO}/commits/HEAD\" --jq .sha 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\"\n       tag_sha=\"$(gh api \"repos/${REPO}/commits/${tag}\" --jq .sha 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\"\n       if [ -n \"$head_sha\" ] && [ -n \"$tag_sha\" ] && [ \"$head_sha\" != \"$tag_sha\" ]; then\n         echo \"::notice title=Healing build of an existing tag::Packaging ${tag}, which is not the tip of the default branch. ...\"\n       fi\n     fi\n     ```\n\n   - **`tests/unit/ci-cd/workflow_release.rs`** — two tests added before `release_workflow_jobs_have_explicit_timeouts`: `releases_do_not_publish_past_a_failing_secrets_scan_or_e2e_suite` (asserts both release jobs declare each gate in `needs` and compare `!= 'failure'`, filtering out comment lines) and `lint_job_gates_on_workflow_shell_and_clippy_findings` (asserts `-D warnings`, `actionlint`, `shellcheck --severity=warning`).\n\n   - **`REQUIREMENTS.md`** — R474 amended (artifact/lockfile exclusion, 94.20% of `v0.300.0..main`); R478 amended (Report at release, Enforce+differential at PR gate, named the covering tests); R480 added (METRIC_VERSION epochs).\n\n   - **`changelog.d/20260720_150000_issue_812_ci_false_positives.md`** — NEW, `bump: patch`, with Fixed/Added sections covering all of the above.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n   - `sudo apt-get install -y shellcheck` failed (exit 1) → downloaded the static binary `shellcheck-v0.10.0.linux.x86_64.tar.xz` to `/tmp/shellcheck` instead.\n   - A `sleep 60; tail ...` chain was blocked by the harness → replaced with `until grep -q \"test result:\" <file>; do sleep 5; done`.\n   - Two concurrent `cargo test --test unit` background runs deadlocked on the cargo build-directory lock (both reported exit 144 after `pkill -f \"cargo test\"`) → killed both and started a single run writing to `ci-logs/unit-tests.log` (background ID `b0t3mkm7h`).\n   - An early `grep -rn ... .` appeared to show `simulate-fresh-merge.sh` had no caller in this repo's workflows; re-grepping `.github/workflows/` explicitly showed it IS called at release.yml:317 and :540. The tool (ugrep) skips hidden directories by default. The F2 finding was still valid but narrower: only `desktop-release.yml` lacked it.\n   - Verified actionlint genuinely type-checks by injecting `needs.secrets-scanX` into a copy — it errored, confirming the real file's expressions are validated.\n   - No user feedback or corrections were received at any point (only one user message exists in the entire conversation).\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n\n   **Defect A (from before compaction, already committed as `e80d47ee`)** — `Auto Release` deadlocked on the self-hosting ratchet. Two root causes, both fixed and verified: (1) the denominator measured log volume — 599,340 of 636,240 lines (94.20%) in `v0.300.0..main` were captured CI transcripts the repo requires each iteration to commit; fixed by symmetric exclusion of captured artifacts + lockfiles with `METRIC_VERSION = 2` starting a new comparison epoch. (2) enforcement sat where nobody could act (on `main`, after commits were immutable, blocking the only thing that moves the range); fixed with `RatchetPolicy::Report` at release time and a differential `--check-ratchet` PR gate. Verified: the exact failing command now exits 0 → `4.36% (1608/36896 changed lines; 10/119 commits)`.\n\n   **Defect B** — macOS codesign failure is a `workflow_run` healing build of tag v0.300.0, which predates the four merged packaging fixes; the fixed code is proven green (PR run 29746221627: `considered=1479 skipped=751`). No `desktop/` change needed — it needs a newer tag, which Defect A's fix unblocks. This session added the `::notice` so a red healing build is self-explaining rather than re-diagnosed.\n\n   **This session's sweep (all verified locally):** the size gate never saw a workflow (`.git` substring); clippy never gated (no `-D warnings`); releases could publish past a failing secrets scan or E2E suite; the desktop `finalize` job could clobber a complete checksum manifest on cancel; desktop packaging validated a stale merge preview; `node --test $(ls | grep)` could silently run zero tests; secretlint floated to `latest`; `$BASE_REF` was unquoted; nothing linted the pipeline definitions or the shipped shell scripts at all.\n\n   Final verification state: `actionlint -shellcheck=/tmp/shellcheck -pyflakes=` → EXIT=0 across all workflows; `shellcheck --severity=warning` over 17 shipped scripts → EXIT=0; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` → OK; `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` → EXIT=0; `rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs` → EXIT=0; `ci_cd::check_file_size` 14/14 pass; `ci_cd::desktop_release_resolve` 10/10 pass.\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/812 / Your prepared branch: issue-812-7f9674a82402 / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/813 — Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813 folder. Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help. If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off. If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code. Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them. Proceed.\"\n   - A final instruction to produce this summary as text only, with no tool calls.\n   - (No other user messages. All background-task notifications explicitly state they are NOT user input and must not be treated as approval.)\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   - #1 Collect CI evidence into `dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813` — DONE (committed `e80d47ee`)\n   - #2 Fix self-hosting metric denominator — DONE (committed, verified)\n   - #3 Move ratchet enforcement to where it is actionable — DONE (committed, verified)\n   - #4 Fix macOS desktop codesign failure — root cause established, unblocked by #2/#3; healing-build `::notice` added this session; the optional unverified `overrides: {\"@electron/osx-sign\": \"^2.6.0\"}` pin remains undecided\n   - #5 Apply CI/CD template sweep findings — essentially complete, UNCOMMITTED\n   - #6 Analysis (done), regression tests (done), changelog fragment (done), REQUIREMENTS.md (done); still to do: confirm the full `cargo test --test unit` run, commit + push, update PR 813 description, `gh pr ready 813`\n   - Still pending: file the two drafted upstream issues against the python template (no workflow-level `permissions:`; redundant `always() && !cancelled()` at `:105`, `:186`, `:517`), and an upstream report for the `simulate-fresh-merge.sh` unquoted `$BASE_REF` in the js template\n   - `dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis.md` should be updated to record which sweep findings were applied and how\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n\n   I was finishing the second atomic commit (the template/CI sweep). Everything listed in §3 is edited on disk but **nothing from this session is committed yet**. The immediately preceding action was adding the healing-build `::notice` to `scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh::emit_outputs()` and verifying it:\n   ```\n   /tmp/shellcheck --severity=warning scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh; echo \"EXIT=$?\"  →  EXIT=0\n   cargo test --test unit ci_cd::desktop_release_resolve  →  10 passed; 0 failed\n   ```\n   A full `cargo test --test unit` run is in flight in the background (ID `b0t3mkm7h`, output to `ci-logs/unit-tests.log`) and its result has NOT yet been read. That run is the gate before committing, because the new assertions in `tests/unit/ci-cd/workflow_release.rs` and the `needs:` changes in `release.yml` could interact with existing workflow-structure tests (e.g. `release_workflow_jobs_have_explicit_timeouts`, `change_gated_jobs_never_depend_on_a_skipped_changelog`).\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n\n   Read `ci-logs/unit-tests.log` (background task `b0t3mkm7h`) to confirm the full unit suite passes, fix any test that the `needs:`/`if:` changes broke, then commit and push this second atomic change to `issue-812-7f9674a82402` with the required `Formal-AI-Session` / `Formal-AI-Evidence` trailers.\n\n   This continues directly from the last action. The immediately prior verification was: \"`/tmp/shellcheck --severity=warning scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh; echo \"EXIT=$?\"` → `EXIT=0`\" and \"`test result: ok. 10 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 1945 filtered out`\", and the full-suite run was started with the command `cargo test --test unit > ci-logs/unit-tests.log 2>&1; echo \"EXIT=$?\" >> ci-logs/unit-tests.log` after killing the two deadlocked duplicate runs.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1784567326843/c4748e71-547e-4463-9222-6d60ed734129.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
