[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]     "model": "claude-opus-4-8",
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]     "id": "msg_011CdDn47Q24VF8N1DXo95kV",
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]     "type": "message",
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]     "role": "assistant",
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]     "content": [
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]       {
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]         "type": "tool_use",
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]         "id": "toolu_018pwjhTQwkQHSqAFT7re1EQ",
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]         "name": "Bash",
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]         "input": {
[2026-07-20T18:24:40.892Z] [INFO]           "command": "git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(ci): close the false-positive and false-negative gaps across the pipeline\n\nIssue #812 asks for every false positive, false negative, warning and\nerror in CI/CD. The second class -- checks that pass without checking --\nturned out to be the larger one. Each item below was reproduced locally\nbefore it was fixed.\n\nChecks that never gated:\n\n* `cargo clippy` ran without `-D warnings`. Every lint in `[lints.clippy]`\n  is `warn`, so the job printed findings and exited 0. The tree is clean\n  today, so this promotes existing behaviour rather than adding failures.\n* `scripts/check-file-size.rs` matched its directory exclusions as\n  substrings, so `.git` hid `.github/workflows/**` from the size gate\n  entirely. Exclusions are now per path component, and workflows are\n  measured (warn 1500, fail 2000) while third-party workflows quoted\n  under `docs/case-studies/**` stay exempt.\n* Nothing validated the workflow definitions or the shipped shell\n  scripts. A mistyped `needs.<job>` reference fails *open* -- the guarded\n  step silently skips under a green check. actionlint (with shellcheck)\n  and shellcheck now run in `lint`.\n* `node --test $(ls … | grep -v …)` fell back to Node's own discovery if\n  the glob stopped matching, i.e. a green step running none of the\n  intended tests. The list is built explicitly and an empty list errors.\n\nChecks that gated the wrong thing:\n\n* `auto-release`/`manual-release` needed only `[lint, test, build]`, so a\n  red `Secrets Scan` or E2E suite on `main` still published the crate,\n  the Docker image and the GitHub Release.\n* The desktop `finalize` job ran under `always()`, letting a cancelled\n  run clobber a complete `SHA256SUMS.txt` with a partial one.\n* Desktop packaging and VS Code jobs validated a stale merge preview;\n  they now simulate the fresh merge as `lint`/`test` already did.\n* `secretlint` floated to whatever `latest` was at run time; pinned.\n* `$BASE_REF` was unquoted in `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh`.\n\nA healing build of an existing tag now says so with a `::notice`: run\n29752745259 failed macOS signing on v0.300.0, which predates the four\nmerged packaging fixes, and read as \"packaging is broken\" when it meant\n\"the last tag is old\".\n\nVerified: actionlint over all workflows exits 0; shellcheck\n--severity=warning over the 17 shipped scripts exits 0; cargo fmt,\ncargo clippy -D warnings and check-file-size.rs exit 0; the full unit\nsuite passes 1953/1953 with four new regression tests.\n\nFormal-AI-Session: issue-812-claude-20260720\nFormal-AI-Evidence: dev/log/issues/812/pulls/813/analysis.md\nEOF\ngit log -1 --stat --format='%h %s'",
