[2026-07-20T18:26:05.236Z] [INFO]         "content": "35 CI: contradictory always() && !cancelled() guards, no Docker PR gate, missing fresh-merge simulation and secrets scan\n34 codecov/codecov-action pinned to deprecated @v4 (current is v7)\n33 release.yml has no top-level permissions: block, so jobs inherit the default GITHUB_TOKEN scope\n32 Upgrade setup-python and Codecov actions for Node 24 runners\n28 Suppress Git default-branch checkout warning in release workflow\n27 Gate Codecov upload to avoid hidden coverage failures\n26 Make GitHub Pages deployment opt-in until Pages is configured\n24 Add warning threshold annotations to file size check\n21 Support multi-language monorepos: auto-detect layout, namespace release tags/titles, badge the artifact\n20 Release pipeline lacks an install-from-package smoke test (indexing check is not enough)\n18 Manual release can be skipped after workflow_dispatch skips detect-changes\n16 Cap generated GitHub release notes before release creation\n12 docs.yml: bump outdated GitHub Actions (checkout@v4, upload-pages-artifact@v3, deploy-pages@v4) to match the rest of the template fleet\n11 CI: release.yml uses outdated action versions, lacks timeout-minutes on every job, and uses literal cancel-in-progress: true\n9 Track parity for browser-commander preview-regeneration pattern\n8 Add GitHub Pages docs deployment workflow (parity with JS/Rust templates)\n6 create_github_release.py sets release title to bare \"v${version}\" and never adds a PyPI badge\n4 Apply best practices from https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/18\n3 Переписать схему, которая в корне schemas.py с учетом pydantic\n1 Make similar template to https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template by for Python\n=== JS\n106 CI: Dockerfile is only built after publish, so a broken image cannot fail a pull request\n105 publish-to-npm.mjs republishes on a verification miss: registry propagation lag turns a successful release into a publish conflict\n104 release.yml has no top-level permissions: block, so jobs inherit the default GITHUB_TOKEN scope\n103 Do not repeat unchanged no-changelog-comments warnings on every run\n99 Suppress Git default-branch checkout warning in release workflow\n98 Harden generated preview-image pushes against non-fast-forward races\n97 Avoid expected npm 404 and always-auth warning noise in release logs\n95 Exclude Vite source HTML from raw lychee link checks\n93 Code is not a change log\n91 Detect real merge pushes with first-parent diff\n87 merge-changesets silently drops malformed changesets (warn-and-skip loses bump/notes)\n86 check-changesets counts any .md file as a changeset (stray docs poison release detection)\n85 extractReleaseNotes regex lacks end-anchor: '1.2' matches the '1.2.3' section\n82 Support multi-language monorepos: auto-detect layout, namespace release tags/titles, badge the artifact\n81 Release pipeline lacks an install-from-package smoke test (indexing check is not enough)\n79 CI: `test` job runs the full suite on non-code changes (skipped changelog/changeset-check is treated as 'run tests')\n77 publish-to-npm.mjs retries permanent failures and there is no first-publish bootstrap path\n75 CI: buildx boot in publish-dockerhub pulls moby/buildkit from Docker Hub with no mirror fallback — transient registry outage fails publishing\n73 ci: links.yml is missing a concurrency block (redundant runs not cancelled on new commits)\n71 Cap generated GitHub release notes before API release creation\n69 preview-regen: guard Playwright Chromium install with timeout+retry and cache (CDN can stall with no internal timeout)\n67 ci: enforce line limits for JavaScript and Markdown files\n66 Support Bun/Linux-only JavaScript test CI\n64 CI: cancel-in-progress condition is reversed, and preview-regen job lacks failure-artifact upload\n62 Add release-time hook that regenerates example-app screenshots with browser-commander\n60 Document the one-time \"Settings → Pages → Source = GitHub Actions\" prerequisite\n58 Fixes and improvements\n56 Fully support GitHub Pages and Electron/Capacitor Desktop and Mobile apps examples building\n54 Add optional Docker Hub publishing tied to npm releases\n52 create-github-release.mjs sets release name to tag — produces titles like \"js-v0.3.5\" instead of \"[JavaScript] 0.3.5\"\nShell cwd was reset to /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784567326843",
